window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b023-0cd4b6ba64200b38.json"]={sha256:"0cd4b6ba64200b38dfb6bc5acc09ee36b3414a841764d5bedacc226f18941eb9",value:{"id":"b023","title":"上海中心大廈","titleEn":"Shanghai Tower","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從 120° 扭轉外形帶來的 24% 風載折減與上海軟土的長週期地震需求出發，計算 C70 巨柱的軸壓比與雙層外伸桁架的斜桿力，再處理圓形地下連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置、鋼平台爬模與超高泵送、後注漿長樁驗證、性能設計的層間變位檢核，最後是懸掛式外層帷幕與超高速電梯鋼索在營運期的維護。","summaryEn":"Starting from the 24% wind-load reduction of the 120° twisting form and the long-period seismic demand of Shanghai's soft ground, compute the axial-load ratio of C70 mega-columns and diagonal forces in two-storey outriggers, then handle the circular diaphragm wall and single 6 m mat pour, steel-platform climbing forms and extreme pumping, proof of post-grouted long piles and performance-based drift checks, ending with in-service upkeep of the hung outer façade and ropes of ultra-fast elevators.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-supertall","subcategoryTitle":"超高層建築巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"Supertall building landmarks","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-supertall","learningTags":["structures","st-supertall","tower"],"architectureFamily":"tower","architectureNodes":[["鋼筋混凝土核心筒","Reinforced concrete core"],["巨柱與角柱","Mega-columns and corner columns"],["外伸桁架與帶狀桁架","Outrigger and belt trusses"],["懸掛式外層帷幕","Hung outer façade"],["筏基、連續壁與後注漿樁","Mat, diaphragm wall and post-grouted piles"],["電梯與監測介面","Elevator and monitoring interface"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,2],[2,1],[2,3],[1,4],[0,4],[0,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tower","labels":["鋼筋混凝土核心筒","巨柱與角柱","外伸桁架與帶狀桁架","懸掛式外層帷幕","筏基、連續壁與後注漿樁"],"labelsEn":["Reinforced concrete core","Mega-columns and corner columns","Outrigger and belt trusses","Hung outer façade","Mat, diaphragm wall and post-grouted piles"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"外形與巨柱連動練習：某超高層矩形對照方案的基底彎矩 M₀ = 30 GN·m，扭轉外形使風載折減 24%，M = 22.8 GN·m。外伸臂把 60% 傾覆彎矩交給巨柱，受拉與受壓側巨柱群力臂 50 m、每側 3 支巨柱：未扭轉時 ΔN = 0.6×30,000/(50×3) = 120 MN，扭轉後 ΔN = 0.6×22,800/(50×3) ≈ 91.2 MN。巨柱斷面 18.0 m²、含鋼率 4.5%，軸壓比分母 31.8×17.19 + 295×0.81 ≈ 786 MN；重力軸力 400 MN 時，未扭轉 μ = 520/786 ≈ 0.66，超過 0.65 限值，扭轉後 μ = 491.2/786 ≈ 0.63，符合要求。也就是說，外形帶來的風載折減可能決定巨柱是否需要加大；若不改外形而改為增加鋼骨，分母須達 520/0.65 = 800 MN，約需多出 (800 − 786)/(295 − 31.8) ≈ 0.055 m² 鋼骨，含鋼率由 4.5% 升到約 4.8%。數值為教學假設，不代表上海中心的設計值。","textEn":"Form and mega-column exercise: a rectangular comparison scheme has base moment M₀ = 30 GN·m, and a twisting form cuts wind load by 24% to M = 22.8 GN·m. Outriggers pass 60% of overturning to the mega-columns, with 50 m between tension and compression groups and 3 columns per side: without the twist ΔN = 0.6×30,000/(50×3) = 120 MN, with it ΔN = 0.6×22,800/(50×3) ≈ 91.2 MN. For an 18.0 m² mega-column with 4.5% steel, the axial-ratio denominator is 31.8×17.19 + 295×0.81 ≈ 786 MN; with 400 MN of gravity load the untwisted case gives μ = 520/786 ≈ 0.66, above the 0.65 limit, while the twisted case gives μ = 491.2/786 ≈ 0.63, which complies. The form-driven wind reduction can therefore decide whether the mega-columns must grow; keeping the form and adding steel instead requires a denominator of 520/0.65 = 800 MN, or about (800 − 786)/(295 − 31.8) ≈ 0.055 m² of extra steel, raising the steel ratio from 4.5% to about 4.8%. Values are teaching assumptions, not Shanghai Tower's design values.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b023-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減」與「軟土場址與長週期地震需求」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut\" and \"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b023-v13-01","title":"扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「120° 扭轉外形」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “120-degree twist” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海中心大廈的外層帷幕以圓角三角形平面隨高度旋轉約 120°，並逐漸縮小，外緣還有一道垂直凹槽。旋轉與漸縮讓不同高度的迎風寬度與分離點不斷改變，渦流無法沿高度同步脫落；設計者公開說明，經風洞試驗優化外形後，結構風載比同高度的矩形建築約少 24%，結構材料因此減輕。風載減少會沿著外伸臂、巨柱與基礎一路傳遞成材料節省。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「120° 扭轉外形」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shanghai Tower's outer façade is a rounded triangle in plan that rotates about 120° up the height while tapering, with a vertical notch along one edge. Rotation and taper keep changing the windward width and separation points with height, so vortices cannot shed coherently along the tower; the designers report that wind-tunnel refinement of the form cut structural wind loads by about 24% compared with a rectangular building of the same height, lightening the structure. The reduction carries through the outriggers, mega-columns and foundations as material savings. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “120-degree twist” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若矩形對照方案基底彎矩 M₀ = 30 GN·m，24% 折減後 M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If a rectangular comparison scheme has a base moment M₀ = 30 GN·m, a 24% reduction gives M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m.","failure":"常見誤解：「扭轉外形純粹是造型，結構只是被動配合。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The twisting form is purely aesthetic and the structure merely follows.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「120° 扭轉外形」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “120-degree twist”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-01-k1","title":"扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減","titleEn":"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut","text":"上海中心大廈的外層帷幕以圓角三角形平面隨高度旋轉約 120°，並逐漸縮小，外緣還有一道垂直凹槽。旋轉與漸縮讓不同高度的迎風寬度與分離點不斷改變，渦流無法沿高度同步脫落；設計者公開說明，經風洞試驗優化外形後，結構風載比同高度的矩形建築約少 24%，結構材料因此減輕。","textEn":"Shanghai Tower's outer façade is a rounded triangle in plan that rotates about 120° up the height while tapering, with a vertical notch along one edge. Rotation and taper keep changing the windward width and separation points with height, so vortices cannot shed coherently along the tower; the designers report that wind-tunnel refinement of the form cut structural wind loads by about 24% compared with a rectangular building of the same height, lightening the structure.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：扭轉外形純粹是造型，結構只是被動配合。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The twisting form is purely aesthetic and the structure merely follows. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut\" is correct?","options":["扭轉外形純粹是造型，結構只是被動配合。","上海中心大廈的外層帷幕以圓角三角形平面隨高度旋轉約 120°，並逐漸縮小，外緣還有一道垂直凹槽。","建築週期越長，地震力就越小，所以超高層不必擔心地震。"],"optionsEn":["The twisting form is purely aesthetic and the structure merely follows.","Shanghai Tower's outer façade is a rounded triangle in plan that rotates about 120° up the height while tapering, with a vertical notch along one edge.","The longer the building period the smaller the earthquake force, so supertall towers need not worry about earthquakes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"上海中心大廈的外層帷幕以圓角三角形平面隨高度旋轉約 120°，並逐漸縮小，外緣還有一道垂直凹槽。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shanghai Tower's outer façade is a rounded triangle in plan that rotates about 120° up the height while tapering, with a vertical notch along one edge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b023-v13-02","title":"扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減：定量估算","titleEn":"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「120° 扭轉外形」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “120-degree twist” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若矩形對照方案基底彎矩 M₀ = 30 GN·m，24% 折減後 M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m。若外伸臂把 60% 傾覆彎矩交給巨柱、受拉與受壓側巨柱群力臂 50 m，每側巨柱群的軸力變化由 0.6×30,000/50 = 360 MN 降為 0.6×22,800/50 ≈ 274 MN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If a rectangular comparison scheme has a base moment M₀ = 30 GN·m, a 24% reduction gives M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m. If outriggers pass 60% of overturning to the mega-columns with 50 m between tension and compression groups, the axial change per column group falls from 0.6×30,000/50 = 360 MN to 0.6×22,800/50 ≈ 274 MN. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較多種旋轉角度與漸縮率的風洞力平衡試驗，取各風向的基底彎矩與頂層加速度，確認選定外形的折減在所有風向成立而非只在單一方向；再把最終風載輸入結構模型，檢查外伸臂與巨柱內力是否同步下降。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare force-balance wind-tunnel tests for several rotation angles and taper rates, taking base moments and top-floor accelerations for every wind direction to confirm the reduction holds in all directions and not just one; then put the final wind loads into the structural model and check that outrigger and mega-column forces fall accordingly.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若矩形對照方案基底彎矩 M₀ = 30 GN·m，24% 折減後 M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m。若外伸臂把 60% 傾覆彎矩交給巨柱、受拉與受壓側巨柱群力臂 50 m，每側巨柱群的軸力變化由 0.6×30,000/50 = 360 MN 降為 0.6×22,800/50 ≈ 274 MN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"If a rectangular comparison scheme has a base moment M₀ = 30 GN·m, a 24% reduction gives M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m. If outriggers pass 60% of overturning to the mega-columns with 50 m between tension and compression groups, the axial change per column group falls from 0.6×30,000/50 = 360 MN to 0.6×22,800/50 ≈ 274 MN. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut\", which statement holds?","options":["外伸桁架只要在鋼構範圍內設計，核心牆不用另外處理。","鋼平台是剛硬的鋼構，所以和下方混凝土的強度無關。","若矩形對照方案基底彎矩 M₀ = 30 GN·m，24% 折減後 M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m。"],"optionsEn":["Outrigger trusses can be designed within the steelwork alone without special treatment of the core walls.","A steel platform is rigid steelwork, so it does not depend on the strength of the concrete below.","If a rectangular comparison scheme has a base moment M₀ = 30 GN·m, a 24% reduction gives M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若矩形對照方案基底彎矩 M₀ = 30 GN·m，24% 折減後 M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If a rectangular comparison scheme has a base moment M₀ = 30 GN·m, a 24% reduction gives M = 30×0.76 = 22.8 GN·m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b023-v13-03","title":"扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「120° 扭轉外形」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “120-degree twist” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較多種旋轉角度與漸縮率的風洞力平衡試驗，取各風向的基底彎矩與頂層加速度，確認選定外形的折減在所有風向成立而非只在單一方向；再把最終風載輸入結構模型，檢查外伸臂與巨柱內力是否同步下降。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare force-balance wind-tunnel tests for several rotation angles and taper rates, taking base moments and top-floor accelerations for every wind direction to confirm the reduction holds in all directions and not just one; then put the final wind loads into the structural model and check that outrigger and mega-column forces fall accordingly. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把旋轉角、漸縮率與凹槽尺寸列為「受控外形參數」，任何變更都須經風工程與結構顧問重新評估；風洞報告須逐風向列出結果，並說明對照方案的定義。","observationEn":"Site practice: Treat rotation angle, taper rate and notch size as controlled form parameters that cannot change without reassessment by the wind and structural consultants; the wind-tunnel report must list results by wind direction and define the comparison scheme.","failure":"注意干擾：若只在一個主風向比較外形，可能漏掉某個斜向風造成的較大扭轉或橫風反應；若後期為了樓層效率修改旋轉角而未重做風洞，原先的 24% 折減就不再有依據，結構可能在設計風載下不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing forms in only one principal wind direction can miss larger torsional or across-wind response from an oblique wind; changing the rotation later for floor efficiency without repeating wind-tunnel tests removes the basis for the 24% reduction and can leave the structure short under design wind. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較多種旋轉角度與漸縮率的風洞力平衡試驗，取各風向的基底彎矩與頂層加速度，確認選定外形的折減在所有風向成立而非只在單一方向；再把最終風載輸入結構模型，檢查外伸臂與巨柱內力是否同步下降。","textEn":"Compare force-balance wind-tunnel tests for several rotation angles and taper rates, taking base moments and top-floor accelerations for every wind direction to confirm the reduction holds in all directions and not just one; then put the final wind loads into the structural model and check that outrigger and mega-column forces fall accordingly.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把旋轉角、漸縮率與凹槽尺寸列為「受控外形參數」，任何變更都須經風工程與結構顧問重新評估；風洞報告須逐風向列出結果，並說明對照方案的定義。","textEn":"Treat rotation angle, taper rate and notch size as controlled form parameters that cannot change without reassessment by the wind and structural consultants; the wind-tunnel report must list results by wind direction and define the comparison scheme.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut\"?","options":["比較多種旋轉角度與漸縮率的風洞力平衡試驗，取各風向的基底彎矩與頂層加速度，確認選定外形的折減在所有風向成立而非只在單一方向。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","大震後結構完全不能有任何降伏才算設計成功。"],"optionsEn":["Compare force-balance wind-tunnel tests for several rotation angles and taper rates, taking base moments and top-floor accelerations for every wind direction to confirm the reduction holds in all directions and not just one.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A design succeeds only if nothing yields at all in a major earthquake."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較多種旋轉角度與漸縮率的風洞力平衡試驗，取各風向的基底彎矩與頂層加速度，確認選定外形的折減在所有風向成立而非只在單一方向；再把最終風載輸入結構模型，檢查外伸臂與巨柱內力是否同步下降。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare force-balance wind-tunnel tests for several rotation angles and taper rates, taking base moments and top-floor accelerations for every wind direction to confirm the reduction holds in all directions and not just one; then put the final wind loads into the structural model and check that outrigger and mega-column forces fall accordingly. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b023-v13-04","title":"扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減：失效診斷","titleEn":"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「120° 扭轉外形」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “120-degree twist” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只在一個主風向比較外形，可能漏掉某個斜向風造成的較大扭轉或橫風反應；若後期為了樓層效率修改旋轉角而未重做風洞，原先的 24% 折減就不再有依據，結構可能在設計風載下不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing forms in only one principal wind direction can miss larger torsional or across-wind response from an oblique wind; changing the rotation later for floor efficiency without repeating wind-tunnel tests removes the basis for the 24% reduction and can leave the structure short under design wind. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：風載減少會沿著外伸臂、巨柱與基礎一路傳遞成材料節省。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The reduction carries through the outriggers, mega-columns and foundations as material savings.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「扭轉外形純粹是造型，結構只是被動配合。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The twisting form is purely aesthetic and the structure merely follows.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只在一個主風向比較外形，可能漏掉某個斜向風造成的較大扭轉或橫風反應；若後期為了樓層效率修改旋轉角而未重做風洞，原先的 24% 折減就不再有依據，結構可能在設計風載下不足。","textEn":"Comparing forms in only one principal wind direction can miss larger torsional or across-wind response from an oblique wind; changing the rotation later for floor efficiency without repeating wind-tunnel tests removes the basis for the 24% reduction and can leave the structure short under design wind.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「扭轉漸縮外形與 24% 風載折減」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Twisting tapered form and a 24% wind-load cut\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只在一個主風向比較外形，可能漏掉某個斜向風造成的較大扭轉或橫風反應。","建築週期越長，地震力就越小，所以超高層不必擔心地震。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Comparing forms in only one principal wind direction can miss larger torsional or across-wind response from an oblique wind.","The longer the building period the smaller the earthquake force, so supertall towers need not worry about earthquakes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只在一個主風向比較外形，可能漏掉某個斜向風造成的較大扭轉或橫風反應；若後期為了樓層效率修改旋轉角而未重做風洞，原先的 24% 折減就不再有依據，結構可能在設計風載下不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing forms in only one principal wind direction can miss larger torsional or across-wind response from an oblique wind; changing the rotation later for floor efficiency without repeating wind-tunnel tests removes the basis for the 24% reduction and can leave the structure short under design wind. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b023-v13-05","title":"軟土場址與長週期地震需求：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「第四類軟土場址」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Site class IV soft ground” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海浦東位於深厚的軟弱沖積層上，設計者指出場址屬中國規範的第四類場地，接近美國 IBC 的 F 類軟土。軟土會放大長週期的地震動，而超高層的基本週期常在數秒以上，因此地震雖不如風那樣頻繁，卻可能主導核心連梁、外伸臂與巨柱的部分需求。上海中心採用性能化耐震設計，以多組時間歷程檢核大震下的變位、連梁降伏程度與外伸桁架是否保持彈性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「第四類軟土場址」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pudong in Shanghai sits on deep, soft alluvial deposits; the designers report that the site is class IV in the Chinese code, close to class F soft soil in the IBC. Soft ground amplifies long-period earthquake motion, while supertall fundamental periods are often several seconds or more, so earthquakes, though rarer than strong winds, can govern some demands on core link beams, outriggers and mega-columns. Shanghai Tower used performance-based seismic design, checking drift, link-beam yielding and whether the outrigger trusses stay elastic under several time histories in the major earthquake. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Site class IV soft ground” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：場址週期 T_s = 4H/V_s：軟土厚 H = 100 m、平均剪力波速 V_s = 250 m/s 時 T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Site period T_s = 4H/V_s: with H = 100 m of soft deposits and an average shear-wave velocity V_s = 250 m/s, T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「建築週期越長，地震力就越小，所以超高層不必擔心地震。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The longer the building period the smaller the earthquake force, so supertall towers need not worry about earthquakes.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「第四類軟土場址」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Site class IV soft ground”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-05-k1","title":"軟土場址與長週期地震需求","titleEn":"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand","text":"上海浦東位於深厚的軟弱沖積層上，設計者指出場址屬中國規範的第四類場地，接近美國 IBC 的 F 類軟土。軟土會放大長週期的地震動，而超高層的基本週期常在數秒以上，因此地震雖不如風那樣頻繁，卻可能主導核心連梁、外伸臂與巨柱的部分需求。","textEn":"Pudong in Shanghai sits on deep, soft alluvial deposits; the designers report that the site is class IV in the Chinese code, close to class F soft soil in the IBC. Soft ground amplifies long-period earthquake motion, while supertall fundamental periods are often several seconds or more, so earthquakes, though rarer than strong winds, can govern some demands on core link beams, outriggers and mega-columns.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：建築週期越長，地震力就越小，所以超高層不必擔心地震。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The longer the building period the smaller the earthquake force, so supertall towers need not worry about earthquakes. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軟土場址與長週期地震需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand\" is correct?","options":["建築週期越長，地震力就越小，所以超高層不必擔心地震。","只要巨柱強度足夠，軸壓比高一點也沒關係。","上海浦東位於深厚的軟弱沖積層上，設計者指出場址屬中國規範的第四類場地，接近美國 IBC 的 F 類軟土。"],"optionsEn":["The longer the building period the smaller the earthquake force, so supertall towers need not worry about earthquakes.","As long as a mega-column is strong enough, a somewhat high axial-load ratio does not matter.","Pudong in Shanghai sits on deep, soft alluvial deposits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"上海浦東位於深厚的軟弱沖積層上，設計者指出場址屬中國規範的第四類場地，接近美國 IBC 的 F 類軟土。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pudong in Shanghai sits on deep, soft alluvial deposits; the designers report that the site is class IV in the Chinese code, close to class F soft soil in the IBC. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b023-v13-06","title":"軟土場址與長週期地震需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「第四類軟土場址」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Site class IV soft ground” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：場址週期 T_s = 4H/V_s：軟土厚 H = 100 m、平均剪力波速 V_s = 250 m/s 時 T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s。若建築基本週期 T₁ = 9 s、譜加速度 S_a = 0.03 g，譜位移 S_d = S_a·T²/(4π²) = 0.03×9.81×81/39.5 ≈ 0.60 m。週期遠離場址週期，但長週期位移仍很大。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Site period T_s = 4H/V_s: with H = 100 m of soft deposits and an average shear-wave velocity V_s = 250 m/s, T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s. If the building period T₁ = 9 s and spectral acceleration S_a = 0.03 g, spectral displacement S_d = S_a·T²/(4π²) = 0.03×9.81×81/39.5 ≈ 0.60 m. The period is far from the site period, yet the long-period displacement remains large. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以場址鑽探與波速量測建立土層模型，做一維場址反應分析取得地表譜；選用含長週期成分的地震紀錄做時間歷程分析，並把長週期段的譜值與規範設計譜比較，確認選用紀錄沒有低估數秒以上的能量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build a soil model from site borings and shear-wave velocity measurements and run one-dimensional site-response analysis for the surface spectrum; select records with long-period content for time-history analysis and compare their long-period spectral values with the code spectrum, confirming that the chosen records do not underestimate energy beyond a few seconds.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"場址週期 T_s = 4H/V_s：軟土厚 H = 100 m、平均剪力波速 V_s = 250 m/s 時 T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s。若建築基本週期 T₁ = 9 s、譜加速度 S_a = 0.03 g，譜位移 S_d = S_a·T²/(4π²) = 0.03×9.81×81/39.5 ≈ 0.60 m。週期遠離場址週期，但長週期位移仍很大。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Site period T_s = 4H/V_s: with H = 100 m of soft deposits and an average shear-wave velocity V_s = 250 m/s, T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s. If the building period T₁ = 9 s and spectral acceleration S_a = 0.03 g, spectral displacement S_d = S_a·T²/(4π²) = 0.03×9.81×81/39.5 ≈ 0.60 m. The period is far from the site period, yet the long-period displacement remains large. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軟土場址與長週期地震需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand\", which statement holds?","options":["場址週期 T_s = 4H/V_s：軟土厚 H = 100 m、平均剪力波速 V_s = 250 m/s 時 T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s。","圓形連續壁只是為了配合圓形建築外形。","樁端注漿只是補救施工缺陷，正常的樁不需要。"],"optionsEn":["Site period T_s = 4H/V_s: with H = 100 m of soft deposits and an average shear-wave velocity V_s = 250 m/s, T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s.","A circular diaphragm wall is simply chosen to match the round building outline.","Base grouting is only a fix for construction defects and sound piles do not need it."],"answer":0,"explanation":"場址週期 T_s = 4H/V_s：軟土厚 H = 100 m、平均剪力波速 V_s = 250 m/s 時 T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Site period T_s = 4H/V_s: with H = 100 m of soft deposits and an average shear-wave velocity V_s = 250 m/s, T_s = 4×100/250 = 1.6 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b023-v13-07","title":"軟土場址與長週期地震需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「第四類軟土場址」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Site class IV soft ground” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以場址鑽探與波速量測建立土層模型，做一維場址反應分析取得地表譜；選用含長週期成分的地震紀錄做時間歷程分析，並把長週期段的譜值與規範設計譜比較，確認選用紀錄沒有低估數秒以上的能量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build a soil model from site borings and shear-wave velocity measurements and run one-dimensional site-response analysis for the surface spectrum; select records with long-period content for time-history analysis and compare their long-period spectral values with the code spectrum, confirming that the chosen records do not underestimate energy beyond a few seconds. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：性能化設計報告要明列各級地震的性能目標、選用紀錄與其來源、長週期譜的比對，以及同儕審查意見；地震紀錄的選取與調幅須在分析前經審查同意。","observationEn":"Site practice: The performance-based design report should state the performance targets for each earthquake level, the selected records and their sources, the long-period spectral comparison and the peer-review comments; record selection and scaling must be agreed by the reviewers before analysis.","failure":"注意干擾：若只用短週期為主的地震紀錄做分析，長週期位移與連梁轉角會被低估；軟土上的高樓在遠震時也可能出現長時間的晃動，影響電梯運轉與非結構構件。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Analysing only with short-period-dominated records underestimates long-period displacement and link-beam rotation; tall buildings on soft ground can also shake for a long time in distant earthquakes, disrupting elevators and non-structural components. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以場址鑽探與波速量測建立土層模型，做一維場址反應分析取得地表譜；選用含長週期成分的地震紀錄做時間歷程分析，並把長週期段的譜值與規範設計譜比較，確認選用紀錄沒有低估數秒以上的能量。","textEn":"Build a soil model from site borings and shear-wave velocity measurements and run one-dimensional site-response analysis for the surface spectrum; select records with long-period content for time-history analysis and compare their long-period spectral values with the code spectrum, confirming that the chosen records do not underestimate energy beyond a few seconds.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"性能化設計報告要明列各級地震的性能目標、選用紀錄與其來源、長週期譜的比對，以及同儕審查意見；地震紀錄的選取與調幅須在分析前經審查同意。","textEn":"The performance-based design report should state the performance targets for each earthquake level, the selected records and their sources, the long-period spectral comparison and the peer-review comments; record selection and scaling must be agreed by the reviewers before analysis.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軟土場址與長週期地震需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以場址鑽探與波速量測建立土層模型，做一維場址反應分析取得地表譜。","帷幕牆掛在結構上，只需要考慮自重，不需要處理變形。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Build a soil model from site borings and shear-wave velocity measurements and run one-dimensional site-response analysis for the surface spectrum.","A hung curtain wall only needs to carry its own weight and need not deal with movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以場址鑽探與波速量測建立土層模型，做一維場址反應分析取得地表譜；選用含長週期成分的地震紀錄做時間歷程分析，並把長週期段的譜值與規範設計譜比較，確認選用紀錄沒有低估數秒以上的能量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build a soil model from site borings and shear-wave velocity measurements and run one-dimensional site-response analysis for the surface spectrum; select records with long-period content for time-history analysis and compare their long-period spectral values with the code spectrum, confirming that the chosen records do not underestimate energy beyond a few seconds. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b023-v13-08","title":"軟土場址與長週期地震需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「第四類軟土場址」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Site class IV soft ground” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只用短週期為主的地震紀錄做分析，長週期位移與連梁轉角會被低估；軟土上的高樓在遠震時也可能出現長時間的晃動，影響電梯運轉與非結構構件。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Analysing only with short-period-dominated records underestimates long-period displacement and link-beam rotation; tall buildings on soft ground can also shake for a long time in distant earthquakes, disrupting elevators and non-structural components. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：上海中心採用性能化耐震設計，以多組時間歷程檢核大震下的變位、連梁降伏程度與外伸桁架是否保持彈性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Shanghai Tower used performance-based seismic design, checking drift, link-beam yielding and whether the outrigger trusses stay elastic under several time histories in the major earthquake.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「建築週期越長，地震力就越小，所以超高層不必擔心地震。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The longer the building period the smaller the earthquake force, so supertall towers need not worry about earthquakes.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只用短週期為主的地震紀錄做分析，長週期位移與連梁轉角會被低估；軟土上的高樓在遠震時也可能出現長時間的晃動，影響電梯運轉與非結構構件。","textEn":"Analysing only with short-period-dominated records underestimates long-period displacement and link-beam rotation; tall buildings on soft ground can also shake for a long time in distant earthquakes, disrupting elevators and non-structural components.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軟土場址與長週期地震需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Soft-ground site and long-period seismic demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要巨柱強度足夠，軸壓比高一點也沒關係。","若只用短週期為主的地震紀錄做分析，長週期位移與連梁轉角會被低估；軟土上的高樓在遠震時也可能出現長時間的晃動，影響電梯運轉與非結構構件。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","As long as a mega-column is strong enough, a somewhat high axial-load ratio does not matter.","Analysing only with short-period-dominated records underestimates long-period displacement and link-beam rotation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若只用短週期為主的地震紀錄做分析，長週期位移與連梁轉角會被低估；軟土上的高樓在遠震時也可能出現長時間的晃動，影響電梯運轉與非結構構件。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Analysing only with short-period-dominated records underestimates long-period displacement and link-beam rotation; tall buildings on soft ground can also shake for a long time in distant earthquakes, disrupting elevators and non-structural components. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b023-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制」與「外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns\" and \"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b023-v13-09","title":"型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「C70 巨柱與軸壓比」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “C70 mega-columns and axial-load ratio” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海中心的巨型框架由八支主巨柱與四支角柱（約到第五區為止）組成，巨柱為內含「王」字形鋼骨的型鋼混凝土柱，柱底採 C70 高強度混凝土，含鋼率約 4% 至 5%，並把軸壓比限制在 0.65 以下。軸壓比控制的是柱在地震下的延性：軸壓越高，混凝土越接近壓碎，柱的變形能力越差。鋼骨在工廠預焊，提供施工期的承載與吊裝骨架，也讓柱斷面能隨高度逐段縮小。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「C70 巨柱與軸壓比」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shanghai Tower's mega-frame consists of eight main mega-columns and four corner columns that stop around zone 5. The mega-columns are steel-reinforced concrete built around an internal skeleton of interconnected steel plates and sections, use C70 high-strength concrete at the base with a steel ratio of about 4% to 5%, and keep the axial-load ratio below 0.65. The axial-load ratio governs seismic ductility: the higher the compression, the closer the concrete is to crushing and the less deformation the column can sustain. The steel skeleton is pre-welded in the factory, carries load and serves as the erection frame during construction, and lets the section shrink stage by stage up the tower. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “C70 mega-columns and axial-load ratio” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：軸壓比 μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Axial-load ratio μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a).","failure":"常見誤解：「只要巨柱強度足夠，軸壓比高一點也沒關係。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As long as a mega-column is strong enough, a somewhat high axial-load ratio does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「C70 巨柱與軸壓比」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “C70 mega-columns and axial-load ratio”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-09-k1","title":"型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制","titleEn":"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns","text":"上海中心的巨型框架由八支主巨柱與四支角柱（約到第五區為止）組成，巨柱為內含「王」字形鋼骨的型鋼混凝土柱，柱底採 C70 高強度混凝土，含鋼率約 4% 至 5%，並把軸壓比限制在 0.65 以下。軸壓比控制的是柱在地震下的延性：軸壓越高，混凝土越接近壓碎，柱的變形能力越差。","textEn":"Shanghai Tower's mega-frame consists of eight main mega-columns and four corner columns that stop around zone 5. The mega-columns are steel-reinforced concrete built around an internal skeleton of interconnected steel plates and sections, use C70 high-strength concrete at the base with a steel ratio of about 4% to 5%, and keep the axial-load ratio below 0.65.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要巨柱強度足夠，軸壓比高一點也沒關係。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As long as a mega-column is strong enough, a somewhat high axial-load ratio does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns\" is correct?","options":["上海中心的巨型框架由八支主巨柱與四支角柱（約到第五區為止）組成，巨柱為內含「王」字形鋼骨的型鋼混凝土柱，柱底採 C70 高強度混凝土，含鋼率約 4% 至 5%，並把軸壓比限制在 0.65 以下。","只要巨柱強度足夠，軸壓比高一點也沒關係。","外伸桁架只要在鋼構範圍內設計，核心牆不用另外處理。"],"optionsEn":["Shanghai Tower's mega-frame consists of eight main mega-columns and four corner columns that stop around zone 5.","As long as a mega-column is strong enough, a somewhat high axial-load ratio does not matter.","Outrigger trusses can be designed within the steelwork alone without special treatment of the core walls."],"answer":0,"explanation":"上海中心的巨型框架由八支主巨柱與四支角柱（約到第五區為止）組成，巨柱為內含「王」字形鋼骨的型鋼混凝土柱，柱底採 C70 高強度混凝土，含鋼率約 4% 至 5%，並把軸壓比限制在 0.65 以下。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shanghai Tower's mega-frame consists of eight main mega-columns and four corner columns that stop around zone 5. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b023-v13-10","title":"型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制：定量估算","titleEn":"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「C70 巨柱與軸壓比」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “C70 mega-columns and axial-load ratio” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：軸壓比 μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a)。設斷面 5.0 m × 3.6 m = 18.0 m²、含鋼率 4.5%：A_a = 0.81 m²、A_c = 17.19 m²；C70 設計強度 f_c = 31.8 MPa、鋼 f_a = 295 MPa，分母 = 31.8×17.19 + 295×0.81 ≈ 786 MN；N = 480 MN 時 μ ≈ 0.61 ≤ 0.65。含鋼率降為 4% 時 μ 升為約 0.63。斷面與軸力為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Axial-load ratio μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a). For a 5.0 m × 3.6 m = 18.0 m² section with 4.5% steel, A_a = 0.81 m² and A_c = 17.19 m²; with C70 design strength f_c = 31.8 MPa and steel f_a = 295 MPa, the denominator is 31.8×17.19 + 295×0.81 ≈ 786 MN, so N = 480 MN gives μ ≈ 0.61 ≤ 0.65. At 4% steel μ rises to about 0.63. Section and load are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐區列出巨柱斷面、含鋼率、混凝土強度與重力加地震組合下的軸壓比，確認每一區都低於限值；鋼骨的工廠焊接以超音波檢測，現場則檢查鋼骨與鋼筋的間距是否足以讓混凝土填實，必要時以足尺模型柱試澆並切開檢查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Tabulate mega-column section, steel ratio, concrete strength and axial-load ratio under gravity plus earthquake zone by zone, confirming every zone is below the limit; ultrasonically test the factory welds of the steel skeleton, and on site check that spacing between steel and rebar allows full concrete compaction, using a sliced full-scale mock-up where needed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"軸壓比 μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a)。設斷面 5.0 m × 3.6 m = 18.0 m²、含鋼率 4.5%：A_a = 0.81 m²、A_c = 17.19 m²；C70 設計強度 f_c = 31.8 MPa、鋼 f_a = 295 MPa，分母 = 31.8×17.19 + 295×0.81 ≈ 786 MN；N = 480 MN 時 μ ≈ 0.61 ≤ 0.65。含鋼率降為 4% 時 μ 升為約 0.63。斷面與軸力為教學假設。","textEn":"Axial-load ratio μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a). For a 5.0 m × 3.6 m = 18.0 m² section with 4.5% steel, A_a = 0.81 m² and A_c = 17.19 m²; with C70 design strength f_c = 31.8 MPa and steel f_a = 295 MPa, the denominator is 31.8×17.19 + 295×0.81 ≈ 786 MN, so N = 480 MN gives μ ≈ 0.61 ≤ 0.65. At 4% steel μ rises to about 0.63. Section and load are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼平台是剛硬的鋼構，所以和下方混凝土的強度無關。","軸壓比 μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a)。","大震後結構完全不能有任何降伏才算設計成功。"],"optionsEn":["A steel platform is rigid steelwork, so it does not depend on the strength of the concrete below.","Axial-load ratio μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a).","A design succeeds only if nothing yields at all in a major earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"軸壓比 μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Axial-load ratio μ = N/(f_c·A_c + f_a·A_a). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b023-v13-11","title":"型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「C70 巨柱與軸壓比」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “C70 mega-columns and axial-load ratio” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐區列出巨柱斷面、含鋼率、混凝土強度與重力加地震組合下的軸壓比，確認每一區都低於限值；鋼骨的工廠焊接以超音波檢測，現場則檢查鋼骨與鋼筋的間距是否足以讓混凝土填實，必要時以足尺模型柱試澆並切開檢查。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Tabulate mega-column section, steel ratio, concrete strength and axial-load ratio under gravity plus earthquake zone by zone, confirming every zone is below the limit; ultrasonically test the factory welds of the steel skeleton, and on site check that spacing between steel and rebar allows full concrete compaction, using a sliced full-scale mock-up where needed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：巨柱施工前提出鋼骨、鋼筋與澆置孔的三維綜合圖，確認振動棒或自充填混凝土能到達每個角落；澆置後以超音波或敲擊抽查，結果與軸壓比表一起納入竣工資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Before mega-column work, submit three-dimensional coordination drawings of steel, rebar and placement openings to confirm that vibrators or self-consolidating concrete can reach every corner; after placement spot-check by ultrasonic testing or tapping and include the results with the axial-load ratio table in the as-built records.","failure":"注意干擾：軸壓比過高的巨柱在大震下延性不足，可能出現混凝土壓碎與鋼筋挫屈；鋼骨與鋼筋排列過密時，混凝土在翼板下方形成空洞，實際容量低於計算值且難以從外觀發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mega-columns with too high an axial-load ratio lack ductility in a major earthquake and can suffer concrete crushing and bar buckling; congested steel and rebar leave voids beneath flanges, so the real capacity falls below the calculation without visible signs. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐區列出巨柱斷面、含鋼率、混凝土強度與重力加地震組合下的軸壓比，確認每一區都低於限值；鋼骨的工廠焊接以超音波檢測，現場則檢查鋼骨與鋼筋的間距是否足以讓混凝土填實，必要時以足尺模型柱試澆並切開檢查。","textEn":"Tabulate mega-column section, steel ratio, concrete strength and axial-load ratio under gravity plus earthquake zone by zone, confirming every zone is below the limit; ultrasonically test the factory welds of the steel skeleton, and on site check that spacing between steel and rebar allows full concrete compaction, using a sliced full-scale mock-up where needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"巨柱施工前提出鋼骨、鋼筋與澆置孔的三維綜合圖，確認振動棒或自充填混凝土能到達每個角落；澆置後以超音波或敲擊抽查，結果與軸壓比表一起納入竣工資料。","textEn":"Before mega-column work, submit three-dimensional coordination drawings of steel, rebar and placement openings to confirm that vibrators or self-consolidating concrete can reach every corner; after placement spot-check by ultrasonic testing or tapping and include the results with the axial-load ratio table in the as-built records.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","電梯鋼索擺動是機電問題，和結構設計無關。","逐區列出巨柱斷面、含鋼率、混凝土強度與重力加地震組合下的軸壓比，確認每一區都低於限值。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Elevator rope sway is a mechanical issue unrelated to structural design.","Tabulate mega-column section, steel ratio, concrete strength and axial-load ratio under gravity plus earthquake zone by zone, confirming every zone is below the limit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐區列出巨柱斷面、含鋼率、混凝土強度與重力加地震組合下的軸壓比，確認每一區都低於限值；鋼骨的工廠焊接以超音波檢測，現場則檢查鋼骨與鋼筋的間距是否足以讓混凝土填實，必要時以足尺模型柱試澆並切開檢查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Tabulate mega-column section, steel ratio, concrete strength and axial-load ratio under gravity plus earthquake zone by zone, confirming every zone is below the limit; ultrasonically test the factory welds of the steel skeleton, and on site check that spacing between steel and rebar allows full concrete compaction, using a sliced full-scale mock-up where needed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b023-v13-12","title":"型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「C70 巨柱與軸壓比」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “C70 mega-columns and axial-load ratio” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"軸壓比過高的巨柱在大震下延性不足，可能出現混凝土壓碎與鋼筋挫屈；鋼骨與鋼筋排列過密時，混凝土在翼板下方形成空洞，實際容量低於計算值且難以從外觀發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mega-columns with too high an axial-load ratio lack ductility in a major earthquake and can suffer concrete crushing and bar buckling; congested steel and rebar leave voids beneath flanges, so the real capacity falls below the calculation without visible signs. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鋼骨在工廠預焊，提供施工期的承載與吊裝骨架，也讓柱斷面能隨高度逐段縮小。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The steel skeleton is pre-welded in the factory, carries load and serves as the erection frame during construction, and lets the section shrink stage by stage up the tower.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要巨柱強度足夠，軸壓比高一點也沒關係。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As long as a mega-column is strong enough, a somewhat high axial-load ratio does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"軸壓比過高的巨柱在大震下延性不足，可能出現混凝土壓碎與鋼筋挫屈；鋼骨與鋼筋排列過密時，混凝土在翼板下方形成空洞，實際容量低於計算值且難以從外觀發現。","textEn":"Mega-columns with too high an axial-load ratio lack ductility in a major earthquake and can suffer concrete crushing and bar buckling; congested steel and rebar leave voids beneath flanges, so the real capacity falls below the calculation without visible signs.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「型鋼混凝土巨柱的軸壓比控制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Axial-load ratio control for steel-reinforced concrete mega-columns\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["軸壓比過高的巨柱在大震下延性不足，可能出現混凝土壓碎與鋼筋挫屈；鋼骨與鋼筋排列過密時，混凝土在翼板下方形成空洞，實際容量低於計算值且難以從外觀發現。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","外伸桁架只要在鋼構範圍內設計，核心牆不用另外處理。"],"optionsEn":["Mega-columns with too high an axial-load ratio lack ductility in a major earthquake and can suffer concrete crushing and bar buckling.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Outrigger trusses can be designed within the steelwork alone without special treatment of the core walls."],"answer":0,"explanation":"軸壓比過高的巨柱在大震下延性不足，可能出現混凝土壓碎與鋼筋挫屈；鋼骨與鋼筋排列過密時，混凝土在翼板下方形成空洞，實際容量低於計算值且難以從外觀發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mega-columns with too high an axial-load ratio lack ductility in a major earthquake and can suffer concrete crushing and bar buckling; congested steel and rebar leave voids beneath flanges, so the real capacity falls below the calculation without visible signs. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b023-v13-13","title":"外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「雙層高外伸桁架」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Two-storey outrigger trusses” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海中心沿高度分為九個區，每區 12 至 15 層，區與區之間是兩層高的機電與避難層，內設兩層高的鋼外伸桁架與雙道帶狀桁架；公開資料記載外伸桁架共六道。外伸桁架把核心筒的轉角轉成巨柱軸力，帶狀桁架則把角柱與周邊柱連成整圈，並承接懸掛帷幕的荷重。外伸桁架的弦桿要深入約 30 m 見方的核心筒，核心牆在加強層內以鋼板或型鋼補強，才能承受弦桿傳入的巨大水平力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「雙層高外伸桁架」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shanghai Tower is divided vertically into nine zones of 12 to 15 floors, separated by two-storey mechanical and refuge levels that house two-storey steel outrigger trusses and double belt trusses; public sources record six outrigger levels. The outriggers turn core rotation into mega-column axial force, while the belt trusses tie corner and perimeter columns into a continuous ring and pick up loads from the hung façade. Outrigger chords must penetrate the roughly 30 m square core, whose walls are stiffened with steel plates or sections in the strengthened storeys to take the large horizontal forces delivered by the chords. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Two-storey outrigger trusses” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：外伸桁架斜桿力 F = ΔN/sinθ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Outrigger diagonal force F = ΔN/sinθ.","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸桁架只要在鋼構範圍內設計，核心牆不用另外處理。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Outrigger trusses can be designed within the steelwork alone without special treatment of the core walls.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「雙層高外伸桁架」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Two-storey outrigger trusses”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-13-k1","title":"外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流","titleEn":"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls","text":"上海中心沿高度分為九個區，每區 12 至 15 層，區與區之間是兩層高的機電與避難層，內設兩層高的鋼外伸桁架與雙道帶狀桁架；公開資料記載外伸桁架共六道。外伸桁架把核心筒的轉角轉成巨柱軸力，帶狀桁架則把角柱與周邊柱連成整圈，並承接懸掛帷幕的荷重。","textEn":"Shanghai Tower is divided vertically into nine zones of 12 to 15 floors, separated by two-storey mechanical and refuge levels that house two-storey steel outrigger trusses and double belt trusses; public sources record six outrigger levels. The outriggers turn core rotation into mega-column axial force, while the belt trusses tie corner and perimeter columns into a continuous ring and pick up loads from the hung façade.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸桁架只要在鋼構範圍內設計，核心牆不用另外處理。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Outrigger trusses can be designed within the steelwork alone without special treatment of the core walls. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls\" is correct?","options":["外伸桁架只要在鋼構範圍內設計，核心牆不用另外處理。","上海中心沿高度分為九個區，每區 12 至 15 層，區與區之間是兩層高的機電與避難層，內設兩層高的鋼外伸桁架與雙道帶狀桁架；公開資料記載外伸桁架共六道。","圓形連續壁只是為了配合圓形建築外形。"],"optionsEn":["Outrigger trusses can be designed within the steelwork alone without special treatment of the core walls.","Shanghai Tower is divided vertically into nine zones of 12 to 15 floors, separated by two-storey mechanical and refuge levels that house two-storey steel outrigger trusses and double belt trusses.","A circular diaphragm wall is simply chosen to match the round building outline."],"answer":1,"explanation":"上海中心沿高度分為九個區，每區 12 至 15 層，區與區之間是兩層高的機電與避難層，內設兩層高的鋼外伸桁架與雙道帶狀桁架；公開資料記載外伸桁架共六道。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shanghai Tower is divided vertically into nine zones of 12 to 15 floors, separated by two-storey mechanical and refuge levels that house two-storey steel outrigger trusses and double belt trusses; public sources record six outrigger levels. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b023-v13-14","title":"外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流：定量估算","titleEn":"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙層高外伸桁架」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Two-storey outrigger trusses” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：外伸桁架斜桿力 F = ΔN/sinθ。桁架深 9 m（兩層）、核心到巨柱水平距離 15 m，θ = atan(9/15) ≈ 31.0°、sinθ ≈ 0.514；巨柱軸力變化 ΔN = 60 MN 時 F ≈ 60/0.514 ≈ 117 MN，對應的弦桿水平力 H = ΔN/tanθ = 60/0.6 = 100 MN 要由核心牆吸收。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Outrigger diagonal force F = ΔN/sinθ. For a truss 9 m deep (two storeys) spanning 15 m from core to mega-column, θ = atan(9/15) ≈ 31.0° and sinθ ≈ 0.514; a mega-column axial change ΔN = 60 MN gives F ≈ 60/0.514 ≈ 117 MN, and the corresponding chord force H = ΔN/tanθ = 60/0.6 = 100 MN must be absorbed by the core walls. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿與核心牆接合區的應力與鋼板剪力釘配置，確認力流能在牆內擴散；設計者公開說明在大震分析中外伸與帶狀桁架大多保持彈性，驗證時須同時輸出各道桁架的應力比，確認沒有單一道桁架先行降伏。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check stresses and stud layouts where chords meet the core walls with a local finite-element model, confirming that force spreads into the wall; the designers report that most outrigger and belt trusses stay elastic in the major-earthquake analysis, so verification must output stress ratios for every truss level to confirm that no single level yields first.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"外伸桁架斜桿力 F = ΔN/sinθ。桁架深 9 m（兩層）、核心到巨柱水平距離 15 m，θ = atan(9/15) ≈ 31.0°、sinθ ≈ 0.514；巨柱軸力變化 ΔN = 60 MN 時 F ≈ 60/0.514 ≈ 117 MN，對應的弦桿水平力 H = ΔN/tanθ = 60/0.6 = 100 MN 要由核心牆吸收。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Outrigger diagonal force F = ΔN/sinθ. For a truss 9 m deep (two storeys) spanning 15 m from core to mega-column, θ = atan(9/15) ≈ 31.0° and sinθ ≈ 0.514; a mega-column axial change ΔN = 60 MN gives F ≈ 60/0.514 ≈ 117 MN, and the corresponding chord force H = ΔN/tanθ = 60/0.6 = 100 MN must be absorbed by the core walls. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls\", which statement holds?","options":["樁端注漿只是補救施工缺陷，正常的樁不需要。","帷幕牆掛在結構上，只需要考慮自重，不需要處理變形。","外伸桁架斜桿力 F = ΔN/sinθ。"],"optionsEn":["Base grouting is only a fix for construction defects and sound piles do not need it.","A hung curtain wall only needs to carry its own weight and need not deal with movement.","Outrigger diagonal force F = ΔN/sinθ."],"answer":2,"explanation":"外伸桁架斜桿力 F = ΔN/sinθ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Outrigger diagonal force F = ΔN/sinθ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b023-v13-15","title":"外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙層高外伸桁架」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Two-storey outrigger trusses” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿與核心牆接合區的應力與鋼板剪力釘配置，確認力流能在牆內擴散；設計者公開說明在大震分析中外伸與帶狀桁架大多保持彈性，驗證時須同時輸出各道桁架的應力比，確認沒有單一道桁架先行降伏。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check stresses and stud layouts where chords meet the core walls with a local finite-element model, confirming that force spreads into the wall; the designers report that most outrigger and belt trusses stay elastic in the major-earthquake analysis, so verification must output stress ratios for every truss level to confirm that no single level yields first. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：加強層的鋼構、核心牆鋼板與鋼筋要在同一個三維模型中協調，標示弦桿穿牆處的施工順序與澆置分段；加強層混凝土澆置前設停止點，由結構設計者確認埋件位置與焊接檢驗完成。","observationEn":"Site practice: Coordinate strengthened-storey steel, core-wall plates and rebar in one three-dimensional model, marking the construction sequence and pour breaks where chords pass through the walls; set a hold point before concreting at which the structural designer confirms embed positions and completed weld inspection.","failure":"注意干擾：若弦桿埋入長度不足或核心牆加強不夠，弦桿力會在牆內造成局部壓碎或剪力裂縫，外伸臂的槓桿作用因而失效；帶狀桁架節點若無法容納懸掛帷幕的附加荷重，外層帷幕會出現不均勻下垂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If chord embedment is too short or the core is insufficiently stiffened, chord forces crush or shear-crack the wall locally and the outrigger lever action is lost; belt-truss nodes that cannot take the extra load of the hung façade let the outer skin sag unevenly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿與核心牆接合區的應力與鋼板剪力釘配置，確認力流能在牆內擴散；設計者公開說明在大震分析中外伸與帶狀桁架大多保持彈性，驗證時須同時輸出各道桁架的應力比，確認沒有單一道桁架先行降伏。","textEn":"Check stresses and stud layouts where chords meet the core walls with a local finite-element model, confirming that force spreads into the wall; the designers report that most outrigger and belt trusses stay elastic in the major-earthquake analysis, so verification must output stress ratios for every truss level to confirm that no single level yields first.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"加強層的鋼構、核心牆鋼板與鋼筋要在同一個三維模型中協調，標示弦桿穿牆處的施工順序與澆置分段；加強層混凝土澆置前設停止點，由結構設計者確認埋件位置與焊接檢驗完成。","textEn":"Coordinate strengthened-storey steel, core-wall plates and rebar in one three-dimensional model, marking the construction sequence and pour breaks where chords pass through the walls; set a hold point before concreting at which the structural designer confirms embed positions and completed weld inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls\"?","options":["以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿與核心牆接合區的應力與鋼板剪力釘配置，確認力流能在牆內擴散。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","扭轉外形純粹是造型，結構只是被動配合。"],"optionsEn":["Check stresses and stud layouts where chords meet the core walls with a local finite-element model, confirming that force spreads into the wall.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The twisting form is purely aesthetic and the structure merely follows."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿與核心牆接合區的應力與鋼板剪力釘配置，確認力流能在牆內擴散；設計者公開說明在大震分析中外伸與帶狀桁架大多保持彈性，驗證時須同時輸出各道桁架的應力比，確認沒有單一道桁架先行降伏。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check stresses and stud layouts where chords meet the core walls with a local finite-element model, confirming that force spreads into the wall; the designers report that most outrigger and belt trusses stay elastic in the major-earthquake analysis, so verification must output stress ratios for every truss level to confirm that no single level yields first. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b023-v13-16","title":"外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙層高外伸桁架」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Two-storey outrigger trusses” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若弦桿埋入長度不足或核心牆加強不夠，弦桿力會在牆內造成局部壓碎或剪力裂縫，外伸臂的槓桿作用因而失效；帶狀桁架節點若無法容納懸掛帷幕的附加荷重，外層帷幕會出現不均勻下垂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If chord embedment is too short or the core is insufficiently stiffened, chord forces crush or shear-crack the wall locally and the outrigger lever action is lost; belt-truss nodes that cannot take the extra load of the hung façade let the outer skin sag unevenly. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：外伸桁架的弦桿要深入約 30 m 見方的核心筒，核心牆在加強層內以鋼板或型鋼補強，才能承受弦桿傳入的巨大水平力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Outrigger chords must penetrate the roughly 30 m square core, whose walls are stiffened with steel plates or sections in the strengthened storeys to take the large horizontal forces delivered by the chords.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸桁架只要在鋼構範圍內設計，核心牆不用另外處理。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Outrigger trusses can be designed within the steelwork alone without special treatment of the core walls.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若弦桿埋入長度不足或核心牆加強不夠，弦桿力會在牆內造成局部壓碎或剪力裂縫，外伸臂的槓桿作用因而失效；帶狀桁架節點若無法容納懸掛帷幕的附加荷重，外層帷幕會出現不均勻下垂。","textEn":"If chord embedment is too short or the core is insufficiently stiffened, chord forces crush or shear-crack the wall locally and the outrigger lever action is lost; belt-truss nodes that cannot take the extra load of the hung façade let the outer skin sag unevenly.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外伸桁架、帶狀桁架與核心牆的力流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Force flow through outriggers, belt trusses and core walls\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若弦桿埋入長度不足或核心牆加強不夠，弦桿力會在牆內造成局部壓碎或剪力裂縫，外伸臂的槓桿作用因而失效。","圓形連續壁只是為了配合圓形建築外形。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","If chord embedment is too short or the core is insufficiently stiffened, chord forces crush or shear-crack the wall locally and the outrigger lever action is lost.","A circular diaphragm wall is simply chosen to match the round building outline."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若弦桿埋入長度不足或核心牆加強不夠，弦桿力會在牆內造成局部壓碎或剪力裂縫，外伸臂的槓桿作用因而失效；帶狀桁架節點若無法容納懸掛帷幕的附加荷重，外層帷幕會出現不均勻下垂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If chord embedment is too short or the core is insufficiently stiffened, chord forces crush or shear-crack the wall locally and the outrigger lever action is lost; belt-truss nodes that cannot take the extra load of the hung façade let the outer skin sag unevenly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b023-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置」與「鋼平台爬模與超高泵送」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour\" and \"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b023-v13-17","title":"圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「圓形地下連續壁」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Circular diaphragm wall” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海中心的基坑總面積約 30,000 m²、深約 33 m，其中塔樓區以內徑 121 m 的圓形地下連續壁圍護。圓形壁把側向土水壓轉成環向壓力，像拱一樣自行平衡，可以不設內支撐而大面積開挖，讓筏基與樁頭施工不受支撐干擾。筏基為直徑約 121 m、厚 6 m 的 C50 混凝土，約 60,000 m³ 一次連續澆置，以避免施工縫削弱這塊承受全塔荷重的厚板；巨量混凝土的水化熱與溫度裂縫則要以配比與監測控制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「圓形地下連續壁」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shanghai Tower's foundation excavation covers about 30,000 m² to about 33 m deep, with the tower zone enclosed by a circular diaphragm wall of 121 m inner diameter. A circular wall turns lateral earth and water pressure into hoop compression that balances itself like an arch, so a large area can be excavated without internal struts, leaving the mat and pile-head work unobstructed. The mat is C50 concrete about 121 m across and 6 m thick, about 60,000 m³ placed in one continuous pour to avoid joints weakening a slab that carries the whole tower; hydration heat and thermal cracking of this mass of concrete are controlled by mix design and monitoring. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Circular diaphragm wall” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：圓形壁環向壓力 N = p·R。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Hoop force in a circular wall N = p·R.","failure":"常見誤解：「圓形連續壁只是為了配合圓形建築外形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A circular diaphragm wall is simply chosen to match the round building outline.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「圓形地下連續壁」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Circular diaphragm wall”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-17-k1","title":"圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置","titleEn":"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour","text":"上海中心的基坑總面積約 30,000 m²、深約 33 m，其中塔樓區以內徑 121 m 的圓形地下連續壁圍護。圓形壁把側向土水壓轉成環向壓力，像拱一樣自行平衡，可以不設內支撐而大面積開挖，讓筏基與樁頭施工不受支撐干擾。","textEn":"Shanghai Tower's foundation excavation covers about 30,000 m² to about 33 m deep, with the tower zone enclosed by a circular diaphragm wall of 121 m inner diameter. A circular wall turns lateral earth and water pressure into hoop compression that balances itself like an arch, so a large area can be excavated without internal struts, leaving the mat and pile-head work unobstructed.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：圓形連續壁只是為了配合圓形建築外形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A circular diaphragm wall is simply chosen to match the round building outline. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour\" is correct?","options":["圓形連續壁只是為了配合圓形建築外形。","鋼平台是剛硬的鋼構，所以和下方混凝土的強度無關。","上海中心的基坑總面積約 30,000 m²、深約 33 m，其中塔樓區以內徑 121 m 的圓形地下連續壁圍護。"],"optionsEn":["A circular diaphragm wall is simply chosen to match the round building outline.","A steel platform is rigid steelwork, so it does not depend on the strength of the concrete below.","Shanghai Tower's foundation excavation covers about 30,000 m² to about 33 m deep, with the tower zone enclosed by a circular diaphragm wall of 121 m inner diameter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"上海中心的基坑總面積約 30,000 m²、深約 33 m，其中塔樓區以內徑 121 m 的圓形地下連續壁圍護。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shanghai Tower's foundation excavation covers about 30,000 m² to about 33 m deep, with the tower zone enclosed by a circular diaphragm wall of 121 m inner diameter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b023-v13-18","title":"圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置：定量估算","titleEn":"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「圓形地下連續壁」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Circular diaphragm wall” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：圓形壁環向壓力 N = p·R。開挖底附近側壓 p = 400 kPa、半徑 R = 60.5 m 時 N = 400×60.5 = 24,200 kN/m；壁厚 1.2 m 時平均壓應力約 24,200/1.2 ≈ 20.2 MPa，需高強度混凝土且壁體真圓度要好。若一次澆置 60,000 m³ 費時 63 小時，平均供料約 952 m³/h。側壓、壁厚與時間為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Hoop force in a circular wall N = p·R. With lateral pressure p = 400 kPa near formation level and radius R = 60.5 m, N = 400×60.5 = 24,200 kN/m; for a 1.2 m wall the mean compressive stress is about 24,200/1.2 ≈ 20.2 MPa, calling for strong concrete and a truly circular wall. Placing 60,000 m³ in 63 hours would need about 952 m³/h on average. Pressure, thickness and duration are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：連續壁每一槽段施工後以超音波量測垂直度與壁厚，確認圓形幾何偏差在容許範圍；開挖時監測壁體變形、地下水位與鄰近建物沉陷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Ultrasonically check the verticality and thickness of each diaphragm-wall panel to keep the circular geometry within tolerance, and monitor wall deflection, groundwater and neighbouring settlement during excavation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"圓形壁環向壓力 N = p·R。開挖底附近側壓 p = 400 kPa、半徑 R = 60.5 m 時 N = 400×60.5 = 24,200 kN/m；壁厚 1.2 m 時平均壓應力約 24,200/1.2 ≈ 20.2 MPa，需高強度混凝土且壁體真圓度要好。若一次澆置 60,000 m³ 費時 63 小時，平均供料約 952 m³/h。側壓、壁厚與時間為教學假設。","textEn":"Hoop force in a circular wall N = p·R. With lateral pressure p = 400 kPa near formation level and radius R = 60.5 m, N = 400×60.5 = 24,200 kN/m; for a 1.2 m wall the mean compressive stress is about 24,200/1.2 ≈ 20.2 MPa, calling for strong concrete and a truly circular wall. Placing 60,000 m³ in 63 hours would need about 952 m³/h on average. Pressure, thickness and duration are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour\", which statement holds?","options":["圓形壁環向壓力 N = p·R。","大震後結構完全不能有任何降伏才算設計成功。","電梯鋼索擺動是機電問題，和結構設計無關。"],"optionsEn":["Hoop force in a circular wall N = p·R.","A design succeeds only if nothing yields at all in a major earthquake.","Elevator rope sway is a mechanical issue unrelated to structural design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"圓形壁環向壓力 N = p·R。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Hoop force in a circular wall N = p·R. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b023-v13-19","title":"圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「圓形地下連續壁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Circular diaphragm wall” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"連續壁每一槽段施工後以超音波量測垂直度與壁厚，確認圓形幾何偏差在容許範圍；開挖時監測壁體變形、地下水位與鄰近建物沉陷。筏基澆置時在中心、表面與邊緣埋設溫度計，追蹤內外溫差，並記錄供料速率與分層時間，確認沒有冷縫。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Ultrasonically check the verticality and thickness of each diaphragm-wall panel to keep the circular geometry within tolerance, and monitor wall deflection, groundwater and neighbouring settlement during excavation. During the mat pour embed thermometers at the centre, surface and edges to track the temperature difference, and log supply rate and layer timing to confirm there are no cold joints. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：一次澆置的筏基要有供料、泵送、人力與天候的備援計畫，並訂出「供料中斷超過初凝時間即啟動施工縫處理」的停止條件；溫控措施與允許溫差須經設計者核可。","observationEn":"Site practice: A single-pour mat needs contingency plans for supply, pumping, labour and weather, with a stop rule that a supply break longer than initial set triggers the planned construction-joint procedure; temperature controls and allowable differences require the designer's approval.","failure":"注意干擾：圓形壁若某一槽段偏斜或接頭漏水，環向壓力無法均勻傳遞，局部可能彎曲破壞並引起湧砂；巨量筏基若供料中斷形成冷縫，或內外溫差過大造成貫穿裂縫，都會降低筏基的剪力與防水性能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If one panel of the circular wall is out of line or a joint leaks, hoop compression cannot pass evenly and the wall may fail locally in bending and trigger sand boils; a supply interruption that forms a cold joint in the mat, or an excessive temperature difference that causes through-cracks, reduces the mat's shear capacity and watertightness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"連續壁每一槽段施工後以超音波量測垂直度與壁厚，確認圓形幾何偏差在容許範圍；開挖時監測壁體變形、地下水位與鄰近建物沉陷。筏基澆置時在中心、表面與邊緣埋設溫度計，追蹤內外溫差，並記錄供料速率與分層時間，確認沒有冷縫。","textEn":"Ultrasonically check the verticality and thickness of each diaphragm-wall panel to keep the circular geometry within tolerance, and monitor wall deflection, groundwater and neighbouring settlement during excavation. During the mat pour embed thermometers at the centre, surface and edges to track the temperature difference, and log supply rate and layer timing to confirm there are no cold joints.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"一次澆置的筏基要有供料、泵送、人力與天候的備援計畫，並訂出「供料中斷超過初凝時間即啟動施工縫處理」的停止條件；溫控措施與允許溫差須經設計者核可。","textEn":"A single-pour mat needs contingency plans for supply, pumping, labour and weather, with a stop rule that a supply break longer than initial set triggers the planned construction-joint procedure; temperature controls and allowable differences require the designer's approval.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","連續壁每一槽段施工後以超音波量測垂直度與壁厚，確認圓形幾何偏差在容許範圍；開挖時監測壁體變形、地下水位與鄰近建物沉陷。","建築週期越長，地震力就越小，所以超高層不必擔心地震。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Ultrasonically check the verticality and thickness of each diaphragm-wall panel to keep the circular geometry within tolerance, and monitor wall deflection, groundwater and neighbouring settlement during excavation.","The longer the building period the smaller the earthquake force, so supertall towers need not worry about earthquakes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"連續壁每一槽段施工後以超音波量測垂直度與壁厚，確認圓形幾何偏差在容許範圍；開挖時監測壁體變形、地下水位與鄰近建物沉陷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Ultrasonically check the verticality and thickness of each diaphragm-wall panel to keep the circular geometry within tolerance, and monitor wall deflection, groundwater and neighbouring settlement during excavation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b023-v13-20","title":"圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置：失效診斷","titleEn":"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「圓形地下連續壁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Circular diaphragm wall” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"圓形壁若某一槽段偏斜或接頭漏水，環向壓力無法均勻傳遞，局部可能彎曲破壞並引起湧砂；巨量筏基若供料中斷形成冷縫，或內外溫差過大造成貫穿裂縫，都會降低筏基的剪力與防水性能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If one panel of the circular wall is out of line or a joint leaks, hoop compression cannot pass evenly and the wall may fail locally in bending and trigger sand boils; a supply interruption that forms a cold joint in the mat, or an excessive temperature difference that causes through-cracks, reduces the mat's shear capacity and watertightness. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：筏基為直徑約 121 m、厚 6 m 的 C50 混凝土，約 60,000 m³ 一次連續澆置，以避免施工縫削弱這塊承受全塔荷重的厚板；巨量混凝土的水化熱與溫度裂縫則要以配比與監測控制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The mat is C50 concrete about 121 m across and 6 m thick, about 60,000 m³ placed in one continuous pour to avoid joints weakening a slab that carries the whole tower; hydration heat and thermal cracking of this mass of concrete are controlled by mix design and monitoring.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「圓形連續壁只是為了配合圓形建築外形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A circular diaphragm wall is simply chosen to match the round building outline.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"圓形壁若某一槽段偏斜或接頭漏水，環向壓力無法均勻傳遞，局部可能彎曲破壞並引起湧砂；巨量筏基若供料中斷形成冷縫，或內外溫差過大造成貫穿裂縫，都會降低筏基的剪力與防水性能。","textEn":"If one panel of the circular wall is out of line or a joint leaks, hoop compression cannot pass evenly and the wall may fail locally in bending and trigger sand boils; a supply interruption that forms a cold joint in the mat, or an excessive temperature difference that causes through-cracks, reduces the mat's shear capacity and watertightness.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「圓形連續壁與 6 m 筏基的一次澆置」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The circular diaphragm wall and a single 6 m mat pour\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","鋼平台是剛硬的鋼構，所以和下方混凝土的強度無關。","圓形壁若某一槽段偏斜或接頭漏水，環向壓力無法均勻傳遞，局部可能彎曲破壞並引起湧砂。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A steel platform is rigid steelwork, so it does not depend on the strength of the concrete below.","If one panel of the circular wall is out of line or a joint leaks, hoop compression cannot pass evenly and the wall may fail locally in bending and trigger sand boils."],"answer":2,"explanation":"圓形壁若某一槽段偏斜或接頭漏水，環向壓力無法均勻傳遞，局部可能彎曲破壞並引起湧砂；巨量筏基若供料中斷形成冷縫，或內外溫差過大造成貫穿裂縫，都會降低筏基的剪力與防水性能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If one panel of the circular wall is out of line or a joint leaks, hoop compression cannot pass evenly and the wall may fail locally in bending and trigger sand boils; a supply interruption that forms a cold joint in the mat, or an excessive temperature difference that causes through-cracks, reduces the mat's shear capacity and watertightness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b023-v13-21","title":"鋼平台爬模與超高泵送：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「整體鋼平台爬模」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Integral steel-platform climbing formwork” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海中心的核心筒以整體鋼平台模板系統施工，平台把模板、鋼筋作業面、布料機與材料堆放整合在核心頂部，靠爬升系統支承在已硬化的核心牆上逐層上升。混凝土由地面一次泵送到位，承攬單位公開的單泵送高度包括 C60 約 582 m、C45 約 606 m、C35 約 610 m，並曾把 120 MPa 超高強度混凝土泵送到約 620 m。平台荷重要靠早齡期的核心牆承擔，爬升時機與支承點強度成為施工控制重點。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「整體鋼平台爬模」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shanghai Tower's core was built with an integral steel-platform formwork system that combines forms, rebar working decks, a placing boom and material storage at the top of the core, climbing floor by floor on supports bearing on hardened core walls. Concrete was pumped from ground level in one stage; the contractor reports single-stage pumping heights of about 582 m for C60, about 606 m for C45 and about 610 m for C35, and pumped 120 MPa ultra-high-strength concrete to about 620 m. The platform's load rests on young core walls, so climbing time and support-point strength become key construction controls. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Integral steel-platform climbing formwork” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：平台總重 2,000 t 加施工荷重 300 t，W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN，由 12 個支承點分擔約 1.88 MN；若支承處混凝土爬升時強度 15 MPa、容許承壓取 0.6 倍，所需承壓面積 A = 1.88/(0.6×15) ≈ 0.21 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A platform of 2,000 t plus 300 t of construction load gives W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN, about 1.88 MN at each of 12 supports; if the wall concrete at the supports is 15 MPa when climbing and allowable bearing is 0.6 times that, the required bearing area is A = 1.88/(0.6×15) ≈ 0.21 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼平台是剛硬的鋼構，所以和下方混凝土的強度無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A steel platform is rigid steelwork, so it does not depend on the strength of the concrete below.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「整體鋼平台爬模」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Integral steel-platform climbing formwork”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-21-k1","title":"鋼平台爬模與超高泵送","titleEn":"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping","text":"上海中心的核心筒以整體鋼平台模板系統施工，平台把模板、鋼筋作業面、布料機與材料堆放整合在核心頂部，靠爬升系統支承在已硬化的核心牆上逐層上升。混凝土由地面一次泵送到位，承攬單位公開的單泵送高度包括 C60 約 582 m、C45 約 606 m、C35 約 610 m，並曾把 120 MPa 超高強度混凝土泵送到約 620 m。","textEn":"Shanghai Tower's core was built with an integral steel-platform formwork system that combines forms, rebar working decks, a placing boom and material storage at the top of the core, climbing floor by floor on supports bearing on hardened core walls. Concrete was pumped from ground level in one stage; the contractor reports single-stage pumping heights of about 582 m for C60, about 606 m for C45 and about 610 m for C35, and pumped 120 MPa ultra-high-strength concrete to about 620 m.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼平台是剛硬的鋼構，所以和下方混凝土的強度無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A steel platform is rigid steelwork, so it does not depend on the strength of the concrete below. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼平台爬模與超高泵送」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping\" is correct?","options":["上海中心的核心筒以整體鋼平台模板系統施工，平台把模板、鋼筋作業面、布料機與材料堆放整合在核心頂部，靠爬升系統支承在已硬化的核心牆上逐層上升。","鋼平台是剛硬的鋼構，所以和下方混凝土的強度無關。","樁端注漿只是補救施工缺陷，正常的樁不需要。"],"optionsEn":["Shanghai Tower's core was built with an integral steel-platform formwork system that combines forms, rebar working decks, a placing boom and material storage at the top of the core, climbing floor by floor on supports bearing on hardened core walls.","A steel platform is rigid steelwork, so it does not depend on the strength of the concrete below.","Base grouting is only a fix for construction defects and sound piles do not need it."],"answer":0,"explanation":"上海中心的核心筒以整體鋼平台模板系統施工，平台把模板、鋼筋作業面、布料機與材料堆放整合在核心頂部，靠爬升系統支承在已硬化的核心牆上逐層上升。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shanghai Tower's core was built with an integral steel-platform formwork system that combines forms, rebar working decks, a placing boom and material storage at the top of the core, climbing floor by floor on supports bearing on hardened core walls. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b023-v13-22","title":"鋼平台爬模與超高泵送：定量估算","titleEn":"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「整體鋼平台爬模」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Integral steel-platform climbing formwork” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：平台總重 2,000 t 加施工荷重 300 t，W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN，由 12 個支承點分擔約 1.88 MN；若支承處混凝土爬升時強度 15 MPa、容許承壓取 0.6 倍，所需承壓面積 A = 1.88/(0.6×15) ≈ 0.21 m²。強度不足時只能延後爬升或加大承壓板。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A platform of 2,000 t plus 300 t of construction load gives W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN, about 1.88 MN at each of 12 supports; if the wall concrete at the supports is 15 MPa when climbing and allowable bearing is 0.6 times that, the required bearing area is A = 1.88/(0.6×15) ≈ 0.21 m². With less strength, climbing must wait or bearing plates must grow. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每次爬升前以同條件養護試體或成熟度計確認支承處混凝土強度，檢查支承構件、液壓系統與防墜裝置；平台在強風時須鎖定，並以施工階段分析檢查平台荷重與風力下核心牆的應力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before each climb confirm concrete strength at the supports with field-cured specimens or maturity meters, and check support members, hydraulics and fall arresters; lock the platform in high wind and check core-wall stresses under platform load and wind with a construction-stage analysis.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"平台總重 2,000 t 加施工荷重 300 t，W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN，由 12 個支承點分擔約 1.88 MN；若支承處混凝土爬升時強度 15 MPa、容許承壓取 0.6 倍，所需承壓面積 A = 1.88/(0.6×15) ≈ 0.21 m²。強度不足時只能延後爬升或加大承壓板。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A platform of 2,000 t plus 300 t of construction load gives W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN, about 1.88 MN at each of 12 supports; if the wall concrete at the supports is 15 MPa when climbing and allowable bearing is 0.6 times that, the required bearing area is A = 1.88/(0.6×15) ≈ 0.21 m². With less strength, climbing must wait or bearing plates must grow. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼平台爬模與超高泵送」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping\", which statement holds?","options":["帷幕牆掛在結構上，只需要考慮自重，不需要處理變形。","平台總重 2,000 t 加施工荷重 300 t，W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN，由 12 個支承點分擔約 1.88 MN。","扭轉外形純粹是造型，結構只是被動配合。"],"optionsEn":["A hung curtain wall only needs to carry its own weight and need not deal with movement.","A platform of 2,000 t plus 300 t of construction load gives W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN, about 1.88 MN at each of 12 supports.","The twisting form is purely aesthetic and the structure merely follows."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平台總重 2,000 t 加施工荷重 300 t，W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN，由 12 個支承點分擔約 1.88 MN；若支承處混凝土爬升時強度 15 MPa、容許承壓取 0.6 倍，所需承壓面積 A = 1.88/(0.6×15) ≈ 0.21 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A platform of 2,000 t plus 300 t of construction load gives W = 2,300×9.81 ≈ 22.6 MN, about 1.88 MN at each of 12 supports; if the wall concrete at the supports is 15 MPa when climbing and allowable bearing is 0.6 times that, the required bearing area is A = 1.88/(0.6×15) ≈ 0.21 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b023-v13-23","title":"鋼平台爬模與超高泵送：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「整體鋼平台爬模」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Integral steel-platform climbing formwork” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每次爬升前以同條件養護試體或成熟度計確認支承處混凝土強度，檢查支承構件、液壓系統與防墜裝置；平台在強風時須鎖定，並以施工階段分析檢查平台荷重與風力下核心牆的應力。泵送則記錄每段高度的壓力與出口性質，並抽驗強度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before each climb confirm concrete strength at the supports with field-cured specimens or maturity meters, and check support members, hydraulics and fall arresters; lock the platform in high wind and check core-wall stresses under platform load and wind with a construction-stage analysis. For pumping, log pressure and discharge properties at each height band and sample strength. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：平台設計須由專業工程師簽證，施工計畫列出爬升的強度門檻、風速停工條件與緊急鎖定程序；每次爬升設停止點，由現場結構工程師簽核後才可啟動液壓系統。","observationEn":"Site practice: The platform design must be certified by a professional engineer, and the construction plan lists climbing strength thresholds, wind stop limits and emergency locking procedures; set a hold point for every climb so the hydraulics start only after the site structural engineer signs off.","failure":"注意干擾：若在支承處混凝土強度不足時爬升，局部承壓破壞可能使平台傾斜甚至墜落；泵送高強度混凝土時配比黏度或溫度控制不當，會造成堵管，使樓層澆置中斷並形成冷縫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Climbing with insufficient concrete strength at the supports can cause local bearing failure, tilting or even dropping the platform; poor control of viscosity or temperature when pumping high-strength concrete leads to blockages that interrupt a floor pour and leave cold joints. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每次爬升前以同條件養護試體或成熟度計確認支承處混凝土強度，檢查支承構件、液壓系統與防墜裝置；平台在強風時須鎖定，並以施工階段分析檢查平台荷重與風力下核心牆的應力。泵送則記錄每段高度的壓力與出口性質，並抽驗強度。","textEn":"Before each climb confirm concrete strength at the supports with field-cured specimens or maturity meters, and check support members, hydraulics and fall arresters; lock the platform in high wind and check core-wall stresses under platform load and wind with a construction-stage analysis. For pumping, log pressure and discharge properties at each height band and sample strength.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"平台設計須由專業工程師簽證，施工計畫列出爬升的強度門檻、風速停工條件與緊急鎖定程序；每次爬升設停止點，由現場結構工程師簽核後才可啟動液壓系統。","textEn":"The platform design must be certified by a professional engineer, and the construction plan lists climbing strength thresholds, wind stop limits and emergency locking procedures; set a hold point for every climb so the hydraulics start only after the site structural engineer signs off.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼平台爬模與超高泵送」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只要巨柱強度足夠，軸壓比高一點也沒關係。","每次爬升前以同條件養護試體或成熟度計確認支承處混凝土強度，檢查支承構件、液壓系統與防墜裝置。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","As long as a mega-column is strong enough, a somewhat high axial-load ratio does not matter.","Before each climb confirm concrete strength at the supports with field-cured specimens or maturity meters, and check support members, hydraulics and fall arresters."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每次爬升前以同條件養護試體或成熟度計確認支承處混凝土強度，檢查支承構件、液壓系統與防墜裝置；平台在強風時須鎖定，並以施工階段分析檢查平台荷重與風力下核心牆的應力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before each climb confirm concrete strength at the supports with field-cured specimens or maturity meters, and check support members, hydraulics and fall arresters; lock the platform in high wind and check core-wall stresses under platform load and wind with a construction-stage analysis. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b023-v13-24","title":"鋼平台爬模與超高泵送：失效診斷","titleEn":"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「整體鋼平台爬模」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Integral steel-platform climbing formwork” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若在支承處混凝土強度不足時爬升，局部承壓破壞可能使平台傾斜甚至墜落；泵送高強度混凝土時配比黏度或溫度控制不當，會造成堵管，使樓層澆置中斷並形成冷縫。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Climbing with insufficient concrete strength at the supports can cause local bearing failure, tilting or even dropping the platform; poor control of viscosity or temperature when pumping high-strength concrete leads to blockages that interrupt a floor pour and leave cold joints. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平台荷重要靠早齡期的核心牆承擔，爬升時機與支承點強度成為施工控制重點。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The platform's load rests on young core walls, so climbing time and support-point strength become key construction controls.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼平台是剛硬的鋼構，所以和下方混凝土的強度無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A steel platform is rigid steelwork, so it does not depend on the strength of the concrete below.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若在支承處混凝土強度不足時爬升，局部承壓破壞可能使平台傾斜甚至墜落；泵送高強度混凝土時配比黏度或溫度控制不當，會造成堵管，使樓層澆置中斷並形成冷縫。","textEn":"Climbing with insufficient concrete strength at the supports can cause local bearing failure, tilting or even dropping the platform; poor control of viscosity or temperature when pumping high-strength concrete leads to blockages that interrupt a floor pour and leave cold joints.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼平台爬模與超高泵送」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Steel-platform climbing formwork and extreme pumping\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若在支承處混凝土強度不足時爬升，局部承壓破壞可能使平台傾斜甚至墜落；泵送高強度混凝土時配比黏度或溫度控制不當，會造成堵管，使樓層澆置中斷並形成冷縫。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","樁端注漿只是補救施工缺陷，正常的樁不需要。"],"optionsEn":["Climbing with insufficient concrete strength at the supports can cause local bearing failure, tilting or even dropping the platform.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Base grouting is only a fix for construction defects and sound piles do not need it."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若在支承處混凝土強度不足時爬升，局部承壓破壞可能使平台傾斜甚至墜落；泵送高強度混凝土時配比黏度或溫度控制不當，會造成堵管，使樓層澆置中斷並形成冷縫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Climbing with insufficient concrete strength at the supports can cause local bearing failure, tilting or even dropping the platform; poor control of viscosity or temperature when pumping high-strength concrete leads to blockages that interrupt a floor pour and leave cold joints. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b023-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證」與「性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting\" and \"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b023-v13-25","title":"軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「後注漿長鑽掘樁」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post-grouted long bored piles” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海軟土缺乏淺層堅硬持力層，塔樓以大量長鑽掘樁支承，設計者文章記載為 947 支直徑 1 m、長 52 至 56 m 的鑽掘樁（各資料的支數略有出入），承攬單位指出採用超長鑽掘樁並在樁端後注漿，單樁設計承載可達約 1,000 公噸。樁端後注漿是在混凝土硬化後，經預埋管把水泥漿壓入樁底，填實沉渣並預壓樁底土層，提高端承與底部側摩擦，同時減少沉陷的離散。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「後注漿長鑽掘樁」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shanghai's soft ground has no shallow hard bearing stratum, so the tower stands on many long bored piles; the designers' article records 947 piles of 1 m diameter and 52 to 56 m length (counts vary slightly between sources), and the contractor reports super-long bored piles with base post-grouting and design capacities up to about 1,000 t each. Base post-grouting injects cement grout through pre-installed pipes after the concrete hardens, filling base debris and pre-loading the soil beneath the toe, which raises end bearing and lower-shaft friction and narrows the scatter of settlement. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Post-grouted long bored piles” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b.","failure":"常見誤解：「樁端注漿只是補救施工缺陷，正常的樁不需要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Base grouting is only a fix for construction defects and sound piles do not need it.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「後注漿長鑽掘樁」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Post-grouted long bored piles”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-25-k1","title":"軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證","titleEn":"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting","text":"上海軟土缺乏淺層堅硬持力層，塔樓以大量長鑽掘樁支承，設計者文章記載為 947 支直徑 1 m、長 52 至 56 m 的鑽掘樁（各資料的支數略有出入），承攬單位指出採用超長鑽掘樁並在樁端後注漿，單樁設計承載可達約 1,000 公噸。樁端後注漿是在混凝土硬化後，經預埋管把水泥漿壓入樁底，填實沉渣並預壓樁底土層，提高端承與底部側摩擦，同時減少沉陷的離散。","textEn":"Shanghai's soft ground has no shallow hard bearing stratum, so the tower stands on many long bored piles; the designers' article records 947 piles of 1 m diameter and 52 to 56 m length (counts vary slightly between sources), and the contractor reports super-long bored piles with base post-grouting and design capacities up to about 1,000 t each. Base post-grouting injects cement grout through pre-installed pipes after the concrete hardens, filling base debris and pre-loading the soil beneath the toe, which raises end bearing and lower-shaft friction and narrows the scatter of settlement.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：樁端注漿只是補救施工缺陷，正常的樁不需要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Base grouting is only a fix for construction defects and sound piles do not need it. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting\" is correct?","options":["樁端注漿只是補救施工缺陷，正常的樁不需要。","上海軟土缺乏淺層堅硬持力層，塔樓以大量長鑽掘樁支承，設計者文章記載為 947 支直徑 1 m、長 52 至 56 m 的鑽掘樁（各資料的支數略有出入），承攬單位指出採用超長鑽掘樁並在樁端後注漿，單樁設計承載可達約 1,000 公噸。","大震後結構完全不能有任何降伏才算設計成功。"],"optionsEn":["Base grouting is only a fix for construction defects and sound piles do not need it.","Shanghai's soft ground has no shallow hard bearing stratum, so the tower stands on many long bored piles.","A design succeeds only if nothing yields at all in a major earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"上海軟土缺乏淺層堅硬持力層，塔樓以大量長鑽掘樁支承，設計者文章記載為 947 支直徑 1 m、長 52 至 56 m 的鑽掘樁（各資料的支數略有出入），承攬單位指出採用超長鑽掘樁並在樁端後注漿，單樁設計承載可達約 1,000 公噸。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shanghai's soft ground has no shallow hard bearing stratum, so the tower stands on many long bored piles; the designers' article records 947 piles of 1 m diameter and 52 to 56 m length (counts vary slightly between sources), and the contractor reports super-long bored piles with base post-grouting and design capacities up to about 1,000 t each. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b023-v13-26","title":"軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「後注漿長鑽掘樁」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post-grouted long bored piles” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b。D = 1.0 m、L = 54 m、f_s = 85 kPa：側摩擦 ≈ 14.4 MN；A_b = 0.785 m²，未注漿 q_b = 3 MPa 時端承 2.4 MN、合計 16.8 MN；注漿後 q_b = 6 MPa 時端承 4.7 MN、合計 19.1 MN，安全係數 2 時設計約 9.6 MN（約 975 t）。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b. With D = 1.0 m, L = 54 m and f_s = 85 kPa, shaft friction ≈ 14.4 MN; with A_b = 0.785 m², an ungrouted q_b = 3 MPa adds 2.4 MN for 16.8 MN total, while grouting to q_b = 6 MPa adds 4.7 MN for 19.1 MN, about 9.6 MN (about 975 t) design load at a factor of safety of 2. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每支樁記錄注漿壓力、注漿量與樁頂上抬量，三者須同時達標才算完成；以靜載試驗比較注漿與未注漿試驗樁的荷重—沉陷曲線，並以低應變或聲波透測檢查樁身完整性，結果回饋給群樁沉陷分析。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record grout pressure, grout volume and pile-head uplift for every pile, accepting only when all three meet the criteria; compare load–settlement curves of grouted and ungrouted trial piles in static load tests, check pile integrity by low-strain or sonic logging, and feed the results back into group-settlement analysis.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b。D = 1.0 m、L = 54 m、f_s = 85 kPa：側摩擦 ≈ 14.4 MN；A_b = 0.785 m²，未注漿 q_b = 3 MPa 時端承 2.4 MN、合計 16.8 MN；注漿後 q_b = 6 MPa 時端承 4.7 MN、合計 19.1 MN，安全係數 2 時設計約 9.6 MN（約 975 t）。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b. With D = 1.0 m, L = 54 m and f_s = 85 kPa, shaft friction ≈ 14.4 MN; with A_b = 0.785 m², an ungrouted q_b = 3 MPa adds 2.4 MN for 16.8 MN total, while grouting to q_b = 6 MPa adds 4.7 MN for 19.1 MN, about 9.6 MN (about 975 t) design load at a factor of safety of 2. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting\", which statement holds?","options":["電梯鋼索擺動是機電問題，和結構設計無關。","建築週期越長，地震力就越小，所以超高層不必擔心地震。","Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b。"],"optionsEn":["Elevator rope sway is a mechanical issue unrelated to structural design.","The longer the building period the smaller the earthquake force, so supertall towers need not worry about earthquakes.","Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Q = π·D·L·f_s + A_b·q_b. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b023-v13-27","title":"軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「後注漿長鑽掘樁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post-grouted long bored piles” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每支樁記錄注漿壓力、注漿量與樁頂上抬量，三者須同時達標才算完成；以靜載試驗比較注漿與未注漿試驗樁的荷重—沉陷曲線，並以低應變或聲波透測檢查樁身完整性，結果回饋給群樁沉陷分析。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record grout pressure, grout volume and pile-head uplift for every pile, accepting only when all three meet the criteria; compare load–settlement curves of grouted and ungrouted trial piles in static load tests, check pile integrity by low-strain or sonic logging, and feed the results back into group-settlement analysis. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：注漿規範要訂出最小注漿量、終止壓力與上抬量上限，任何一項異常即停止並由大地顧問判斷；注漿紀錄以樁號編入資料庫，與沉陷監測一起移交業主。","observationEn":"Site practice: The grouting specification sets minimum grout volume, termination pressure and maximum uplift, stopping for the geotechnical consultant's judgement whenever one is abnormal; index grouting records by pile number in a database and hand them to the owner with the settlement monitoring.","failure":"注意干擾：注漿管堵塞或注漿量不足的樁，端承仍受沉渣影響，在群樁中成為偏軟的樁，造成筏基不均勻沉陷；注漿壓力過大則可能使漿液沿樁側上竄或擾動鄰近已完成的樁。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Piles with blocked grout pipes or too little grout still sit on base debris and become soft piles in the group, causing uneven mat settlement; excessive grout pressure can drive grout up the shaft or disturb neighbouring finished piles. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每支樁記錄注漿壓力、注漿量與樁頂上抬量，三者須同時達標才算完成；以靜載試驗比較注漿與未注漿試驗樁的荷重—沉陷曲線，並以低應變或聲波透測檢查樁身完整性，結果回饋給群樁沉陷分析。","textEn":"Record grout pressure, grout volume and pile-head uplift for every pile, accepting only when all three meet the criteria; compare load–settlement curves of grouted and ungrouted trial piles in static load tests, check pile integrity by low-strain or sonic logging, and feed the results back into group-settlement analysis.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"注漿規範要訂出最小注漿量、終止壓力與上抬量上限，任何一項異常即停止並由大地顧問判斷；注漿紀錄以樁號編入資料庫，與沉陷監測一起移交業主。","textEn":"The grouting specification sets minimum grout volume, termination pressure and maximum uplift, stopping for the geotechnical consultant's judgement whenever one is abnormal; index grouting records by pile number in a database and hand them to the owner with the settlement monitoring.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting\"?","options":["每支樁記錄注漿壓力、注漿量與樁頂上抬量，三者須同時達標才算完成。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","外伸桁架只要在鋼構範圍內設計，核心牆不用另外處理。"],"optionsEn":["Record grout pressure, grout volume and pile-head uplift for every pile, accepting only when all three meet the criteria.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Outrigger trusses can be designed within the steelwork alone without special treatment of the core walls."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每支樁記錄注漿壓力、注漿量與樁頂上抬量，三者須同時達標才算完成；以靜載試驗比較注漿與未注漿試驗樁的荷重—沉陷曲線，並以低應變或聲波透測檢查樁身完整性，結果回饋給群樁沉陷分析。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record grout pressure, grout volume and pile-head uplift for every pile, accepting only when all three meet the criteria; compare load–settlement curves of grouted and ungrouted trial piles in static load tests, check pile integrity by low-strain or sonic logging, and feed the results back into group-settlement analysis. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b023-v13-28","title":"軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「後注漿長鑽掘樁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post-grouted long bored piles” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"注漿管堵塞或注漿量不足的樁，端承仍受沉渣影響，在群樁中成為偏軟的樁，造成筏基不均勻沉陷；注漿壓力過大則可能使漿液沿樁側上竄或擾動鄰近已完成的樁。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Piles with blocked grout pipes or too little grout still sit on base debris and become soft piles in the group, causing uneven mat settlement; excessive grout pressure can drive grout up the shaft or disturb neighbouring finished piles. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：樁端後注漿是在混凝土硬化後，經預埋管把水泥漿壓入樁底，填實沉渣並預壓樁底土層，提高端承與底部側摩擦，同時減少沉陷的離散。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Base post-grouting injects cement grout through pre-installed pipes after the concrete hardens, filling base debris and pre-loading the soil beneath the toe, which raises end bearing and lower-shaft friction and narrows the scatter of settlement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「樁端注漿只是補救施工缺陷，正常的樁不需要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Base grouting is only a fix for construction defects and sound piles do not need it.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"注漿管堵塞或注漿量不足的樁，端承仍受沉渣影響，在群樁中成為偏軟的樁，造成筏基不均勻沉陷；注漿壓力過大則可能使漿液沿樁側上竄或擾動鄰近已完成的樁。","textEn":"Piles with blocked grout pipes or too little grout still sit on base debris and become soft piles in the group, causing uneven mat settlement; excessive grout pressure can drive grout up the shaft or disturb neighbouring finished piles.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軟土中的長樁與樁端後注漿驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long piles in soft ground and verification of base post-grouting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","注漿管堵塞或注漿量不足的樁，端承仍受沉渣影響，在群樁中成為偏軟的樁，造成筏基不均勻沉陷；注漿壓力過大則可能使漿液沿樁側上竄或擾動鄰近已完成的樁。","大震後結構完全不能有任何降伏才算設計成功。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Piles with blocked grout pipes or too little grout still sit on base debris and become soft piles in the group, causing uneven mat settlement.","A design succeeds only if nothing yields at all in a major earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"注漿管堵塞或注漿量不足的樁，端承仍受沉渣影響，在群樁中成為偏軟的樁，造成筏基不均勻沉陷；注漿壓力過大則可能使漿液沿樁側上竄或擾動鄰近已完成的樁。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Piles with blocked grout pipes or too little grout still sit on base debris and become soft piles in the group, causing uneven mat settlement; excessive grout pressure can drive grout up the shaft or disturb neighbouring finished piles. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b023-v13-29","title":"性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「七組時間歷程與層間變位」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Seven time histories and storey drift” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海中心的性能化耐震設計以七組地震時間歷程分析，設計者公開的結果是大震下平均最大層間變位角小於 1/130，低於 1/100 的限值；多數核心連梁降伏但仍在「生命安全」性能範圍內，外伸與帶狀桁架大多保持彈性。連梁是刻意設計的耗能元件，讓核心牆的牆肢在大震後仍可修復；外伸桁架則必須保持彈性，因為它一旦降伏，整個巨型框架的勁度分配就會改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「七組時間歷程與層間變位」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shanghai Tower's performance-based seismic design used seven sets of time-history analyses; the designers report an average maximum storey drift angle below 1/130 in the major earthquake, within the 1/100 limit, with most core link beams yielding while staying within the life-safety level and most outrigger and belt trusses remaining elastic. Link beams are intended energy-dissipating elements that keep core wall piers repairable after a major earthquake, whereas the outriggers must stay elastic because once they yield, stiffness distribution across the mega-frame changes. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Seven time histories and storey drift” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：層間變位 Δ = θ·h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Storey drift Δ = θ·h.","failure":"常見誤解：「大震後結構完全不能有任何降伏才算設計成功。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A design succeeds only if nothing yields at all in a major earthquake.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「七組時間歷程與層間變位」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Seven time histories and storey drift”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-29-k1","title":"性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核","titleEn":"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design","text":"上海中心的性能化耐震設計以七組地震時間歷程分析，設計者公開的結果是大震下平均最大層間變位角小於 1/130，低於 1/100 的限值；多數核心連梁降伏但仍在「生命安全」性能範圍內，外伸與帶狀桁架大多保持彈性。連梁是刻意設計的耗能元件，讓核心牆的牆肢在大震後仍可修復；外伸桁架則必須保持彈性，因為它一旦降伏，整個巨型框架的勁度分配就會改變。","textEn":"Shanghai Tower's performance-based seismic design used seven sets of time-history analyses; the designers report an average maximum storey drift angle below 1/130 in the major earthquake, within the 1/100 limit, with most core link beams yielding while staying within the life-safety level and most outrigger and belt trusses remaining elastic. Link beams are intended energy-dissipating elements that keep core wall piers repairable after a major earthquake, whereas the outriggers must stay elastic because once they yield, stiffness distribution across the mega-frame changes.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：大震後結構完全不能有任何降伏才算設計成功。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A design succeeds only if nothing yields at all in a major earthquake. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design\" is correct?","options":["大震後結構完全不能有任何降伏才算設計成功。","帷幕牆掛在結構上，只需要考慮自重，不需要處理變形。","上海中心的性能化耐震設計以七組地震時間歷程分析，設計者公開的結果是大震下平均最大層間變位角小於 1/130，低於 1/100 的限值。"],"optionsEn":["A design succeeds only if nothing yields at all in a major earthquake.","A hung curtain wall only needs to carry its own weight and need not deal with movement.","Shanghai Tower's performance-based seismic design used seven sets of time-history analyses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"上海中心的性能化耐震設計以七組地震時間歷程分析，設計者公開的結果是大震下平均最大層間變位角小於 1/130，低於 1/100 的限值；多數核心連梁降伏但仍在「生命安全」性能範圍內，外伸與帶狀桁架大多保持彈性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shanghai Tower's performance-based seismic design used seven sets of time-history analyses; the designers report an average maximum storey drift angle below 1/130 in the major earthquake, within the 1/100 limit, with most core link beams yielding while staying within the life-safety level and most outrigger and belt trusses remaining elastic. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b023-v13-30","title":"性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核：定量估算","titleEn":"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「七組時間歷程與層間變位」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Seven time histories and storey drift” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：層間變位 Δ = θ·h。樓高 4.5 m 時，θ = 1/130 對應 Δ ≈ 34.6 mm，限值 1/100 對應 45 mm。連梁轉角近似 γ = θ·L/l：牆肢形心距 L = 6 m、連梁淨跨 l = 2 m 時 γ ≈ (1/130)×6/2 ≈ 0.023 rad，須小於該連梁配筋形式在生命安全等級的轉角限值。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Storey drift Δ = θ·h. For a 4.5 m storey, θ = 1/130 gives Δ ≈ 34.6 mm against 45 mm at the 1/100 limit. Link-beam rotation is roughly γ = θ·L/l: with wall-pier centroids L = 6 m apart and a clear span l = 2 m, γ ≈ (1/130)×6/2 ≈ 0.023 rad, which must stay below the life-safety rotation limit for that reinforcement layout. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依規範取七組以上紀錄時以平均值判定，逐層輸出層間變位角、連梁轉角與外伸桁架應力比，並做敏感度分析（例如混凝土勁度折減、阻尼比變化）；設計結論須經超限高層建築專項審查與同儕審查確認。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: With seven or more records, judge on the mean as the code allows; output storey drift angles, link-beam rotations and outrigger stress ratios floor by floor, run sensitivity studies such as cracked-stiffness reductions and damping changes, and have the conclusions confirmed by the special review for code-exceeding tall buildings and by peer review.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"層間變位 Δ = θ·h。樓高 4.5 m 時，θ = 1/130 對應 Δ ≈ 34.6 mm，限值 1/100 對應 45 mm。連梁轉角近似 γ = θ·L/l：牆肢形心距 L = 6 m、連梁淨跨 l = 2 m 時 γ ≈ (1/130)×6/2 ≈ 0.023 rad，須小於該連梁配筋形式在生命安全等級的轉角限值。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Storey drift Δ = θ·h. For a 4.5 m storey, θ = 1/130 gives Δ ≈ 34.6 mm against 45 mm at the 1/100 limit. Link-beam rotation is roughly γ = θ·L/l: with wall-pier centroids L = 6 m apart and a clear span l = 2 m, γ ≈ (1/130)×6/2 ≈ 0.023 rad, which must stay below the life-safety rotation limit for that reinforcement layout. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design\", which statement holds?","options":["層間變位 Δ = θ·h。","扭轉外形純粹是造型，結構只是被動配合。","只要巨柱強度足夠，軸壓比高一點也沒關係。"],"optionsEn":["Storey drift Δ = θ·h.","The twisting form is purely aesthetic and the structure merely follows.","As long as a mega-column is strong enough, a somewhat high axial-load ratio does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"層間變位 Δ = θ·h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Storey drift Δ = θ·h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b023-v13-31","title":"性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「七組時間歷程與層間變位」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Seven time histories and storey drift” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依規範取七組以上紀錄時以平均值判定，逐層輸出層間變位角、連梁轉角與外伸桁架應力比，並做敏感度分析（例如混凝土勁度折減、阻尼比變化）；設計結論須經超限高層建築專項審查與同儕審查確認。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"With seven or more records, judge on the mean as the code allows; output storey drift angles, link-beam rotations and outrigger stress ratios floor by floor, run sensitivity studies such as cracked-stiffness reductions and damping changes, and have the conclusions confirmed by the special review for code-exceeding tall buildings and by peer review. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在結構圖上標示「預期降伏構件」與「須保持彈性構件」，前者訂出可更換或修復的細部，後者訂出超強係數；大震後的檢查清單依此分類，優先檢查連梁與外伸桁架接合。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark on the structural drawings which members are expected to yield and which must stay elastic, giving the former repairable or replaceable details and the latter overstrength factors; organise the post-earthquake checklist the same way, inspecting link beams and outrigger connections first.","failure":"注意干擾：若連梁被設計得過強而不先降伏，地震能量會轉移到牆肢底部或外伸桁架，造成難以修復的損傷；若外伸桁架在大震中降伏，巨柱與核心的分擔改變，變位會突然增加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If link beams are made too strong to yield first, seismic energy shifts to the base of wall piers or to the outriggers, causing damage that is hard to repair; if outriggers yield in a major earthquake, the core–column share changes and drift suddenly increases. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依規範取七組以上紀錄時以平均值判定，逐層輸出層間變位角、連梁轉角與外伸桁架應力比，並做敏感度分析（例如混凝土勁度折減、阻尼比變化）；設計結論須經超限高層建築專項審查與同儕審查確認。","textEn":"With seven or more records, judge on the mean as the code allows; output storey drift angles, link-beam rotations and outrigger stress ratios floor by floor, run sensitivity studies such as cracked-stiffness reductions and damping changes, and have the conclusions confirmed by the special review for code-exceeding tall buildings and by peer review.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在結構圖上標示「預期降伏構件」與「須保持彈性構件」，前者訂出可更換或修復的細部，後者訂出超強係數；大震後的檢查清單依此分類，優先檢查連梁與外伸桁架接合。","textEn":"Mark on the structural drawings which members are expected to yield and which must stay elastic, giving the former repairable or replaceable details and the latter overstrength factors; organise the post-earthquake checklist the same way, inspecting link beams and outrigger connections first.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","依規範取七組以上紀錄時以平均值判定，逐層輸出層間變位角、連梁轉角與外伸桁架應力比，並做敏感度分析（例如混凝土勁度折減、阻尼比變化）。","圓形連續壁只是為了配合圓形建築外形。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","With seven or more records, judge on the mean as the code allows.","A circular diaphragm wall is simply chosen to match the round building outline."],"answer":1,"explanation":"依規範取七組以上紀錄時以平均值判定，逐層輸出層間變位角、連梁轉角與外伸桁架應力比，並做敏感度分析（例如混凝土勁度折減、阻尼比變化）；設計結論須經超限高層建築專項審查與同儕審查確認。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"With seven or more records, judge on the mean as the code allows; output storey drift angles, link-beam rotations and outrigger stress ratios floor by floor, run sensitivity studies such as cracked-stiffness reductions and damping changes, and have the conclusions confirmed by the special review for code-exceeding tall buildings and by peer review. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b023-v13-32","title":"性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「七組時間歷程與層間變位」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seven time histories and storey drift” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若連梁被設計得過強而不先降伏，地震能量會轉移到牆肢底部或外伸桁架，造成難以修復的損傷；若外伸桁架在大震中降伏，巨柱與核心的分擔改變，變位會突然增加。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If link beams are made too strong to yield first, seismic energy shifts to the base of wall piers or to the outriggers, causing damage that is hard to repair; if outriggers yield in a major earthquake, the core–column share changes and drift suddenly increases. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：連梁是刻意設計的耗能元件，讓核心牆的牆肢在大震後仍可修復；外伸桁架則必須保持彈性，因為它一旦降伏，整個巨型框架的勁度分配就會改變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Link beams are intended energy-dissipating elements that keep core wall piers repairable after a major earthquake, whereas the outriggers must stay elastic because once they yield, stiffness distribution across the mega-frame changes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「大震後結構完全不能有任何降伏才算設計成功。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A design succeeds only if nothing yields at all in a major earthquake.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若連梁被設計得過強而不先降伏，地震能量會轉移到牆肢底部或外伸桁架，造成難以修復的損傷；若外伸桁架在大震中降伏，巨柱與核心的分擔改變，變位會突然增加。","textEn":"If link beams are made too strong to yield first, seismic energy shifts to the base of wall piers or to the outriggers, causing damage that is hard to repair; if outriggers yield in a major earthquake, the core–column share changes and drift suddenly increases.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「性能化耐震設計的變位與連梁檢核」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drift and link-beam checks in performance-based seismic design\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","帷幕牆掛在結構上，只需要考慮自重，不需要處理變形。","若連梁被設計得過強而不先降伏，地震能量會轉移到牆肢底部或外伸桁架，造成難以修復的損傷；若外伸桁架在大震中降伏，巨柱與核心的分擔改變，變位會突然增加。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A hung curtain wall only needs to carry its own weight and need not deal with movement.","If link beams are made too strong to yield first, seismic energy shifts to the base of wall piers or to the outriggers, causing damage that is hard to repair."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若連梁被設計得過強而不先降伏，地震能量會轉移到牆肢底部或外伸桁架，造成難以修復的損傷；若外伸桁架在大震中降伏，巨柱與核心的分擔改變，變位會突然增加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If link beams are made too strong to yield first, seismic energy shifts to the base of wall piers or to the outriggers, causing damage that is hard to repair; if outriggers yield in a major earthquake, the core–column share changes and drift suddenly increases. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b023-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護」與「電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade\" and \"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b023-v13-33","title":"懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「柔性懸掛帷幕支撐」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Flexible hung façade supports” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海中心的外層帷幕與內層樓板之間有中庭空間，外層玻璃不能直接固定在樓板邊緣，而是以柔性懸掛系統掛在每區的機電層帶狀桁架下，允許相對主結構在垂直方向自由變形；承攬單位指出曲面帷幕有超過 20,000 片尺寸各異的玻璃，以柔性懸掛結構與向下施工的智慧平台安裝。懸掛系統要同時吸收溫度伸縮、樓層下垂、風壓與層間變位，接縫與滑動件是長期維護的重點。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「柔性懸掛帷幕支撐」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shanghai Tower's outer façade is separated from the floor plates by atrium space, so the outer glass cannot be fixed at slab edges; instead it hangs from the belt trusses at each zone's mechanical level on a flexible suspension system that lets it move vertically relative to the main structure. The contractor reports more than 20,000 glass pieces of different sizes on the curved wall, installed with the flexible suspension and a top-down intelligent platform. The suspension must absorb thermal movement, floor sag, wind pressure and storey drift together, so joints and sliding parts are the focus of long-term upkeep. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Flexible hung façade supports” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：懸掛段的溫度伸縮 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Thermal movement of a hung segment ΔL = α·L·ΔT.","failure":"常見誤解：「帷幕牆掛在結構上，只需要考慮自重，不需要處理變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A hung curtain wall only needs to carry its own weight and need not deal with movement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「柔性懸掛帷幕支撐」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Flexible hung façade supports”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-33-k1","title":"懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護","titleEn":"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade","text":"上海中心的外層帷幕與內層樓板之間有中庭空間，外層玻璃不能直接固定在樓板邊緣，而是以柔性懸掛系統掛在每區的機電層帶狀桁架下，允許相對主結構在垂直方向自由變形；承攬單位指出曲面帷幕有超過 20,000 片尺寸各異的玻璃，以柔性懸掛結構與向下施工的智慧平台安裝。懸掛系統要同時吸收溫度伸縮、樓層下垂、風壓與層間變位，接縫與滑動件是長期維護的重點。","textEn":"Shanghai Tower's outer façade is separated from the floor plates by atrium space, so the outer glass cannot be fixed at slab edges; instead it hangs from the belt trusses at each zone's mechanical level on a flexible suspension system that lets it move vertically relative to the main structure. The contractor reports more than 20,000 glass pieces of different sizes on the curved wall, installed with the flexible suspension and a top-down intelligent platform.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：帷幕牆掛在結構上，只需要考慮自重，不需要處理變形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A hung curtain wall only needs to carry its own weight and need not deal with movement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade\" is correct?","options":["上海中心的外層帷幕與內層樓板之間有中庭空間，外層玻璃不能直接固定在樓板邊緣，而是以柔性懸掛系統掛在每區的機電層帶狀桁架下，允許相對主結構在垂直方向自由變形。","帷幕牆掛在結構上，只需要考慮自重，不需要處理變形。","電梯鋼索擺動是機電問題，和結構設計無關。"],"optionsEn":["Shanghai Tower's outer façade is separated from the floor plates by atrium space, so the outer glass cannot be fixed at slab edges.","A hung curtain wall only needs to carry its own weight and need not deal with movement.","Elevator rope sway is a mechanical issue unrelated to structural design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"上海中心的外層帷幕與內層樓板之間有中庭空間，外層玻璃不能直接固定在樓板邊緣，而是以柔性懸掛系統掛在每區的機電層帶狀桁架下，允許相對主結構在垂直方向自由變形；承攬單位指出曲面帷幕有超過 20,000 片尺寸各異的玻璃，以柔性懸掛結構與向下施工的智慧平台安裝。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shanghai Tower's outer façade is separated from the floor plates by atrium space, so the outer glass cannot be fixed at slab edges; instead it hangs from the belt trusses at each zone's mechanical level on a flexible suspension system that lets it move vertically relative to the main structure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b023-v13-34","title":"懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護：定量估算","titleEn":"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「柔性懸掛帷幕支撐」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Flexible hung façade supports” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：懸掛段的溫度伸縮 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。一區 14 層、每層 4.5 m，懸掛長度 L ≈ 63 m；α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C、ΔT = 40 °C 時 ΔL = 12×10⁻⁶×63,000×40 ≈ 30 mm。底部滑動接頭須容許約 ±30 mm 以上，並另加樓層下垂與施工誤差。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Thermal movement of a hung segment ΔL = α·L·ΔT. A 14-floor zone at 4.5 m per floor hangs about L ≈ 63 m; with α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C and ΔT = 40 °C, ΔL = 12×10⁻⁶×63,000×40 ≈ 30 mm. The bottom sliding joint must allow about ±30 mm or more, plus floor sag and construction tolerances. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以實尺寸試體做垂直往復位移與層間變位試驗，確認滑動接頭不卡死、玻璃不受擠壓；完工後在代表性懸吊桿與滑動件旁設置位移計，比對季節溫差下的實際伸縮，並定期檢查吊桿腐蝕、螺栓鬆脫與密封膠劣化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test full-scale specimens under cyclic vertical movement and storey drift to confirm sliding joints do not bind and glass is not squeezed; after completion fit displacement gauges at representative hangers and sliding parts to compare actual seasonal movement, and inspect periodically for hanger corrosion, bolt loosening and sealant ageing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"懸掛段的溫度伸縮 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。一區 14 層、每層 4.5 m，懸掛長度 L ≈ 63 m；α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C、ΔT = 40 °C 時 ΔL = 12×10⁻⁶×63,000×40 ≈ 30 mm。底部滑動接頭須容許約 ±30 mm 以上，並另加樓層下垂與施工誤差。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Thermal movement of a hung segment ΔL = α·L·ΔT. A 14-floor zone at 4.5 m per floor hangs about L ≈ 63 m; with α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C and ΔT = 40 °C, ΔL = 12×10⁻⁶×63,000×40 ≈ 30 mm. The bottom sliding joint must allow about ±30 mm or more, plus floor sag and construction tolerances. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade\", which statement holds?","options":["建築週期越長，地震力就越小，所以超高層不必擔心地震。","懸掛段的溫度伸縮 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。","外伸桁架只要在鋼構範圍內設計，核心牆不用另外處理。"],"optionsEn":["The longer the building period the smaller the earthquake force, so supertall towers need not worry about earthquakes.","Thermal movement of a hung segment ΔL = α·L·ΔT.","Outrigger trusses can be designed within the steelwork alone without special treatment of the core walls."],"answer":1,"explanation":"懸掛段的溫度伸縮 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Thermal movement of a hung segment ΔL = α·L·ΔT. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b023-v13-35","title":"懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「柔性懸掛帷幕支撐」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Flexible hung façade supports” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以實尺寸試體做垂直往復位移與層間變位試驗，確認滑動接頭不卡死、玻璃不受擠壓；完工後在代表性懸吊桿與滑動件旁設置位移計，比對季節溫差下的實際伸縮，並定期檢查吊桿腐蝕、螺栓鬆脫與密封膠劣化。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test full-scale specimens under cyclic vertical movement and storey drift to confirm sliding joints do not bind and glass is not squeezed; after completion fit displacement gauges at representative hangers and sliding parts to compare actual seasonal movement, and inspect periodically for hanger corrosion, bolt loosening and sealant ageing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件要附懸掛系統的滑動方向圖、容許位移、吊桿與螺栓的檢查週期，以及禁止在滑動件上加裝任何附掛物的規定；破損玻璃更換須依原設計間隙重新調整並記錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover documents should include sliding-direction diagrams, allowable movements, inspection intervals for hangers and bolts, and a rule forbidding any attachment to sliding parts; replacement panes must be re-gapped to the original design clearances and recorded.","failure":"注意干擾：滑動接頭若被灰塵、腐蝕或施工時誤加的固定件卡死，溫度伸縮會轉成玻璃與框架的附加應力，導致玻璃破裂；懸吊桿螺栓鬆脫則可能使整片帷幕下沉，碰撞下方構件。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If sliding joints are jammed by dirt, corrosion or fixings mistakenly added during construction, thermal movement becomes extra stress in glass and frames and cracks the glass; loosened hanger bolts can let a whole façade panel drop and strike members below. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以實尺寸試體做垂直往復位移與層間變位試驗，確認滑動接頭不卡死、玻璃不受擠壓；完工後在代表性懸吊桿與滑動件旁設置位移計，比對季節溫差下的實際伸縮，並定期檢查吊桿腐蝕、螺栓鬆脫與密封膠劣化。","textEn":"Test full-scale specimens under cyclic vertical movement and storey drift to confirm sliding joints do not bind and glass is not squeezed; after completion fit displacement gauges at representative hangers and sliding parts to compare actual seasonal movement, and inspect periodically for hanger corrosion, bolt loosening and sealant ageing.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件要附懸掛系統的滑動方向圖、容許位移、吊桿與螺栓的檢查週期，以及禁止在滑動件上加裝任何附掛物的規定；破損玻璃更換須依原設計間隙重新調整並記錄。","textEn":"Handover documents should include sliding-direction diagrams, allowable movements, inspection intervals for hangers and bolts, and a rule forbidding any attachment to sliding parts; replacement panes must be re-gapped to the original design clearances and recorded.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","鋼平台是剛硬的鋼構，所以和下方混凝土的強度無關。","以實尺寸試體做垂直往復位移與層間變位試驗，確認滑動接頭不卡死、玻璃不受擠壓。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A steel platform is rigid steelwork, so it does not depend on the strength of the concrete below.","Test full-scale specimens under cyclic vertical movement and storey drift to confirm sliding joints do not bind and glass is not squeezed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以實尺寸試體做垂直往復位移與層間變位試驗，確認滑動接頭不卡死、玻璃不受擠壓；完工後在代表性懸吊桿與滑動件旁設置位移計，比對季節溫差下的實際伸縮，並定期檢查吊桿腐蝕、螺栓鬆脫與密封膠劣化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test full-scale specimens under cyclic vertical movement and storey drift to confirm sliding joints do not bind and glass is not squeezed; after completion fit displacement gauges at representative hangers and sliding parts to compare actual seasonal movement, and inspect periodically for hanger corrosion, bolt loosening and sealant ageing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b023-v13-36","title":"懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「柔性懸掛帷幕支撐」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Flexible hung façade supports” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"滑動接頭若被灰塵、腐蝕或施工時誤加的固定件卡死，溫度伸縮會轉成玻璃與框架的附加應力，導致玻璃破裂；懸吊桿螺栓鬆脫則可能使整片帷幕下沉，碰撞下方構件。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If sliding joints are jammed by dirt, corrosion or fixings mistakenly added during construction, thermal movement becomes extra stress in glass and frames and cracks the glass; loosened hanger bolts can let a whole façade panel drop and strike members below. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：懸掛系統要同時吸收溫度伸縮、樓層下垂、風壓與層間變位，接縫與滑動件是長期維護的重點。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The suspension must absorb thermal movement, floor sag, wind pressure and storey drift together, so joints and sliding parts are the focus of long-term upkeep.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「帷幕牆掛在結構上，只需要考慮自重，不需要處理變形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A hung curtain wall only needs to carry its own weight and need not deal with movement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"滑動接頭若被灰塵、腐蝕或施工時誤加的固定件卡死，溫度伸縮會轉成玻璃與框架的附加應力，導致玻璃破裂；懸吊桿螺栓鬆脫則可能使整片帷幕下沉，碰撞下方構件。","textEn":"If sliding joints are jammed by dirt, corrosion or fixings mistakenly added during construction, thermal movement becomes extra stress in glass and frames and cracks the glass; loosened hanger bolts can let a whole façade panel drop and strike members below.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「懸掛式外層帷幕的變位吸收與維護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Movement absorption and upkeep of the hung outer façade\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["滑動接頭若被灰塵、腐蝕或施工時誤加的固定件卡死，溫度伸縮會轉成玻璃與框架的附加應力，導致玻璃破裂；懸吊桿螺栓鬆脫則可能使整片帷幕下沉，碰撞下方構件。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","電梯鋼索擺動是機電問題，和結構設計無關。"],"optionsEn":["If sliding joints are jammed by dirt, corrosion or fixings mistakenly added during construction, thermal movement becomes extra stress in glass and frames and cracks the glass.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Elevator rope sway is a mechanical issue unrelated to structural design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"滑動接頭若被灰塵、腐蝕或施工時誤加的固定件卡死，溫度伸縮會轉成玻璃與框架的附加應力，導致玻璃破裂；懸吊桿螺栓鬆脫則可能使整片帷幕下沉，碰撞下方構件。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If sliding joints are jammed by dirt, corrosion or fixings mistakenly added during construction, thermal movement becomes extra stress in glass and frames and cracks the glass; loosened hanger bolts can let a whole façade panel drop and strike members below. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b023-v13-37","title":"電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「超高速電梯曳引鋼索」如何影響上海中心大廈的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ultra-fast elevator hoist ropes” governs force, deformation or durability in “Shanghai Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"上海中心有 106 部電梯，最高速度 20.5 m/s，超長行程的曳引鋼索與補償鋼索像一條很長的弦，自然頻率隨車廂位置改變。當建築在強風下以數秒以上的週期擺動，若鋼索某一長度的頻率接近建築頻率，鋼索就會在井道內共振擺動，碰撞井道設備或纏繞。這個問題屬於結構與機電的介面：結構提供建築頻率與擺幅，電梯系統依此設定強風時的停靠樓層、降速或暫停營運模式。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「超高速電梯曳引鋼索」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shanghai Tower has 106 elevators with a top speed of 20.5 m/s. Very long hoist and compensation ropes behave like long strings whose natural frequency changes with car position. When the building sways with a period of several seconds in strong wind and some rope length has a frequency near the building's, the rope resonates in the shaft, striking equipment or tangling. This is a structure–services interface: the structure supplies building frequency and amplitude, and the elevator system uses them to set high-wind parking floors, reduced speed or suspended service. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Ultra-fast elevator hoist ropes” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：弦振動頻率 f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: String frequency f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ).","failure":"常見誤解：「電梯鋼索擺動是機電問題，和結構設計無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Elevator rope sway is a mechanical issue unrelated to structural design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「超高速電梯曳引鋼索」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Ultra-fast elevator hoist ropes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-37-k1","title":"電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式","titleEn":"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes","text":"上海中心有 106 部電梯，最高速度 20.5 m/s，超長行程的曳引鋼索與補償鋼索像一條很長的弦，自然頻率隨車廂位置改變。當建築在強風下以數秒以上的週期擺動，若鋼索某一長度的頻率接近建築頻率，鋼索就會在井道內共振擺動，碰撞井道設備或纏繞。","textEn":"Shanghai Tower has 106 elevators with a top speed of 20.5 m/s. Very long hoist and compensation ropes behave like long strings whose natural frequency changes with car position.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：電梯鋼索擺動是機電問題，和結構設計無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Elevator rope sway is a mechanical issue unrelated to structural design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes\" is correct?","options":["電梯鋼索擺動是機電問題，和結構設計無關。","上海中心有 106 部電梯，最高速度 20.5 m/s，超長行程的曳引鋼索與補償鋼索像一條很長的弦，自然頻率隨車廂位置改變。","扭轉外形純粹是造型，結構只是被動配合。"],"optionsEn":["Elevator rope sway is a mechanical issue unrelated to structural design.","Shanghai Tower has 106 elevators with a top speed of 20.5 m/s.","The twisting form is purely aesthetic and the structure merely follows."],"answer":1,"explanation":"上海中心有 106 部電梯，最高速度 20.5 m/s，超長行程的曳引鋼索與補償鋼索像一條很長的弦，自然頻率隨車廂位置改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shanghai Tower has 106 elevators with a top speed of 20.5 m/s. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b023-v13-38","title":"電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式：定量估算","titleEn":"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超高速電梯曳引鋼索」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ultra-fast elevator hoist ropes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：弦振動頻率 f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ)。張力 T = 100 kN、單位質量 μ = 8 kg/m 時波速 √(100,000/8) ≈ 112 m/s；自由長度 L = 500 m 時 f ≈ 112/1,000 ≈ 0.112 Hz，與週期 9 s 的建築頻率 0.111 Hz 幾乎相同；車廂移到中段使 L = 250 m 時 f ≈ 0.224 Hz，可避開共振。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: String frequency f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ). With tension T = 100 kN and mass μ = 8 kg/m the wave speed is √(100,000/8) ≈ 112 m/s; for a free length L = 500 m, f ≈ 112/1,000 ≈ 0.112 Hz, almost equal to the 0.111 Hz of a building with a 9 s period; moving the car to mid-height so that L = 250 m gives f ≈ 0.224 Hz, away from resonance. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以結構模型或實測取得建築前幾個模態頻率與預期擺幅，交給電梯廠商做鋼索擺動模擬；完工後在頂部設加速度計與風速計，連動電梯控制系統，於強風事件後檢查井道內鋼索磨損與設備碰撞痕跡。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Provide the elevator supplier with the building's first few modal frequencies and expected amplitudes from the model or measurements for rope-sway simulation; after completion link rooftop accelerometers and anemometers to the elevator controls, and after high-wind events inspect shafts for rope wear and impact marks on equipment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"弦振動頻率 f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ)。張力 T = 100 kN、單位質量 μ = 8 kg/m 時波速 √(100,000/8) ≈ 112 m/s；自由長度 L = 500 m 時 f ≈ 112/1,000 ≈ 0.112 Hz，與週期 9 s 的建築頻率 0.111 Hz 幾乎相同；車廂移到中段使 L = 250 m 時 f ≈ 0.224 Hz，可避開共振。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"String frequency f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ). With tension T = 100 kN and mass μ = 8 kg/m the wave speed is √(100,000/8) ≈ 112 m/s; for a free length L = 500 m, f ≈ 112/1,000 ≈ 0.112 Hz, almost equal to the 0.111 Hz of a building with a 9 s period; moving the car to mid-height so that L = 250 m gives f ≈ 0.224 Hz, away from resonance. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes\", which statement holds?","options":["只要巨柱強度足夠，軸壓比高一點也沒關係。","圓形連續壁只是為了配合圓形建築外形。","弦振動頻率 f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ)。"],"optionsEn":["As long as a mega-column is strong enough, a somewhat high axial-load ratio does not matter.","A circular diaphragm wall is simply chosen to match the round building outline.","String frequency f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"弦振動頻率 f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"String frequency f = (1/2L)·√(T/μ). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b023-v13-39","title":"電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超高速電梯曳引鋼索」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ultra-fast elevator hoist ropes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以結構模型或實測取得建築前幾個模態頻率與預期擺幅，交給電梯廠商做鋼索擺動模擬；完工後在頂部設加速度計與風速計，連動電梯控制系統，於強風事件後檢查井道內鋼索磨損與設備碰撞痕跡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Provide the elevator supplier with the building's first few modal frequencies and expected amplitudes from the model or measurements for rope-sway simulation; after completion link rooftop accelerometers and anemometers to the elevator controls, and after high-wind events inspect shafts for rope wear and impact marks on equipment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：結構設計者應提供電梯顧問書面的模態頻率、預期擺幅與量測資料，雙方共同訂定強風營運模式的啟動門檻；建築重大改裝或阻尼器調整後，須重新確認這些門檻。","observationEn":"Site practice: The structural designer should give the elevator consultant written modal frequencies, expected amplitudes and measured data, and both should set the trigger thresholds for high-wind operating modes; re-confirm these thresholds after major renovations or damper adjustments.","failure":"注意干擾：若電梯設計沒有考慮建築擺動，強風時鋼索可能在井道內大幅擺動，撞壞導軌支架或纏住樓層設備，造成長時間停駛；乘客受困於高空車廂也會成為緊急救援的難題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the elevator design ignores building sway, ropes can swing widely in strong wind, damaging rail brackets or snagging landing equipment and causing long outages; passengers trapped in cars at height also become a difficult rescue problem. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以結構模型或實測取得建築前幾個模態頻率與預期擺幅，交給電梯廠商做鋼索擺動模擬；完工後在頂部設加速度計與風速計，連動電梯控制系統，於強風事件後檢查井道內鋼索磨損與設備碰撞痕跡。","textEn":"Provide the elevator supplier with the building's first few modal frequencies and expected amplitudes from the model or measurements for rope-sway simulation; after completion link rooftop accelerometers and anemometers to the elevator controls, and after high-wind events inspect shafts for rope wear and impact marks on equipment.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"結構設計者應提供電梯顧問書面的模態頻率、預期擺幅與量測資料，雙方共同訂定強風營運模式的啟動門檻；建築重大改裝或阻尼器調整後，須重新確認這些門檻。","textEn":"The structural designer should give the elevator consultant written modal frequencies, expected amplitudes and measured data, and both should set the trigger thresholds for high-wind operating modes; re-confirm these thresholds after major renovations or damper adjustments.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes\"?","options":["以結構模型或實測取得建築前幾個模態頻率與預期擺幅，交給電梯廠商做鋼索擺動模擬。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","樁端注漿只是補救施工缺陷，正常的樁不需要。"],"optionsEn":["Provide the elevator supplier with the building's first few modal frequencies and expected amplitudes from the model or measurements for rope-sway simulation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Base grouting is only a fix for construction defects and sound piles do not need it."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以結構模型或實測取得建築前幾個模態頻率與預期擺幅，交給電梯廠商做鋼索擺動模擬；完工後在頂部設加速度計與風速計，連動電梯控制系統，於強風事件後檢查井道內鋼索磨損與設備碰撞痕跡。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Provide the elevator supplier with the building's first few modal frequencies and expected amplitudes from the model or measurements for rope-sway simulation; after completion link rooftop accelerometers and anemometers to the elevator controls, and after high-wind events inspect shafts for rope wear and impact marks on equipment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b023-v13-40","title":"電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b023-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超高速電梯曳引鋼索」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ultra-fast elevator hoist ropes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若電梯設計沒有考慮建築擺動，強風時鋼索可能在井道內大幅擺動，撞壞導軌支架或纏住樓層設備，造成長時間停駛；乘客受困於高空車廂也會成為緊急救援的難題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the elevator design ignores building sway, ropes can swing widely in strong wind, damaging rail brackets or snagging landing equipment and causing long outages; passengers trapped in cars at height also become a difficult rescue problem. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這個問題屬於結構與機電的介面：結構提供建築頻率與擺幅，電梯系統依此設定強風時的停靠樓層、降速或暫停營運模式。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This is a structure–services interface: the structure supplies building frequency and amplitude, and the elevator system uses them to set high-wind parking floors, reduced speed or suspended service.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「電梯鋼索擺動是機電問題，和結構設計無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Elevator rope sway is a mechanical issue unrelated to structural design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b023-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若電梯設計沒有考慮建築擺動，強風時鋼索可能在井道內大幅擺動，撞壞導軌支架或纏住樓層設備，造成長時間停駛；乘客受困於高空車廂也會成為緊急救援的難題。","textEn":"If the elevator design ignores building sway, ropes can swing widely in strong wind, damaging rail brackets or snagging landing equipment and causing long outages; passengers trapped in cars at height also become a difficult rescue problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b023-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電梯鋼索共振與強風營運模式」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elevator rope resonance and high-wind operating modes\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若電梯設計沒有考慮建築擺動，強風時鋼索可能在井道內大幅擺動，撞壞導軌支架或纏住樓層設備，造成長時間停駛；乘客受困於高空車廂也會成為緊急救援的難題。","扭轉外形純粹是造型，結構只是被動配合。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","If the elevator design ignores building sway, ropes can swing widely in strong wind, damaging rail brackets or snagging landing equipment and causing long outages.","The twisting form is purely aesthetic and the structure merely follows."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若電梯設計沒有考慮建築擺動，強風時鋼索可能在井道內大幅擺動，撞壞導軌支架或纏住樓層設備，造成長時間停駛；乘客受困於高空車廂也會成為緊急救援的難題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the elevator design ignores building sway, ropes can swing widely in strong wind, damaging rail brackets or snagging landing equipment and causing long outages; passengers trapped in cars at height also become a difficult rescue problem. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-tt-shanghai-tower","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-fem-shanghai-tower-construction","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
